#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2182
msgid "``python_maturin``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2184
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_maturin` class provides support for python-"
"maturin, a replacement for setuptools_rust and another \"backend\" for "
"building Python Wheels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2190
msgid "``python_mesonpy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2192
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_mesonpy` class enables building Python "
"modules which use the meson-python build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2200
msgid "``python_pbr``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2202
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_pbr` class enables building Python projects "
"which use the `Python Build Reasonableness "
"<https://pypi.org/project/pbr/>`__ backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2205
msgid ""
"This class adds ``python3-pbr-native`` to the recipe's build-time "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2212
msgid "``python_pdm``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2214
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_pdm` class adds support for building Python "
"packages with the `PDM <https://pdm-project.org/>`__ package and "
"dependency manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2217
msgid ""
"This class adds  ``python3-pdm-backend-native`` to the recipe's build-"
"time dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2225
msgid "``python_pep517``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2227
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_pep517` class builds and installs a Python "
"``wheel`` binary archive (see `PEP-517 "
"<https://peps.python.org/pep-0517/>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2230
msgid ""
"Recipes wouldn't inherit this directly, instead typically another class "
"will inherit this and add the relevant native dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2233
msgid ""
"Examples of classes which do this are :ref:`ref-classes-"
"python_flit_core`, :ref:`ref-classes-python_setuptools_build_meta`, and "
":ref:`ref-classes-python_poetry_core`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2240
msgid "``python_poetry_core``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2242
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_poetry_core` class enables building Python "
"modules which use the `Poetry Core <https://python-poetry.org>`__ build "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2250
msgid "``python_pyo3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2252
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_pyo3` class helps make sure that Python "
"extensions written in Rust and built with `PyO3 <https://pyo3.rs/>`__, "
"properly set up the environment for cross compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2256
msgid ""
"This class is internal to the :ref:`ref-classes-python-setuptools3_rust` "
"class and is not meant to be used directly in recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2262
msgid "``python_uv_build``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2264
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_uv_build` class can be inherited in Python "
"recipes that are built with ``uv_build`` and which are `PEP-517 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0517/>`__ compliant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2271
msgid "``python-setuptools3_rust``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2273
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python-setuptools3_rust` class enables building "
"Python extensions implemented in Rust with `PyO3 <https://pyo3.rs/>`__, "
"which allows to compile and distribute Python extensions written in Rust "
"as easily as if they were written in C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2278
msgid ""
"This class inherits the :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` and :ref:`ref-"
"classes-python_pyo3` classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2284
msgid "``pixbufcache``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2286
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-pixbufcache` class generates the proper post-"
"install and post-remove (postinst/postrm) scriptlets for packages that "
"install pixbuf loaders, which are used with ``gdk-pixbuf``. These "
"scriptlets call ``update_pixbuf_cache`` to add the pixbuf loaders to the "
"cache. Since the cache files are architecture-specific, "
"``update_pixbuf_cache`` is run using QEMU if the postinst scriptlets need"
" to be run on the build host during image creation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2294
msgid ""
"If the pixbuf loaders being installed are in packages other than the "
"recipe's main package, set :term:`PIXBUF_PACKAGES` to specify the "
"packages containing the loaders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2302 ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:683
msgid "``pkgconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2304
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-pkgconfig` class provides a standard way to get "
"header and library information by using ``pkg-config``. This class aims "
"to smooth integration of ``pkg-config`` into libraries that use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2308
msgid ""
"During staging, BitBake installs ``pkg-config`` data into the "
"``sysroots/`` directory. By making use of sysroot functionality within "
"``pkg-config``, the :ref:`ref-classes-pkgconfig` class no longer has to "
"manipulate the files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2316
msgid "``populate_sdk``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2318
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-populate-sdk` class provides support for SDK-only "
"recipes. For information on advantages gained when building a cross-"
"development toolchain using the :ref:`ref-tasks-populate_sdk` task, see "
"the \":ref:`sdk-manual/appendix-obtain:building an sdk installer`\" "
"section in the Yocto Project Application Development and the Extensible "
"Software Development Kit (eSDK) manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2328
msgid "``populate_sdk_*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2330
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-populate-sdk-*` classes support SDK creation and "
"consist of the following classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2333
msgid ""
":ref:`populate_sdk_base <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`: The base class "
"supporting SDK creation under all package managers (i.e. DEB, RPM, and "
"opkg)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2336
msgid ""
":ref:`populate_sdk_deb <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`: Supports creation "
"of the SDK given the Debian package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2339
msgid ""
":ref:`populate_sdk_rpm <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`: Supports creation "
"of the SDK given the RPM package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2342
msgid ""
":ref:`populate_sdk_ipk <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`: Supports creation "
"of the SDK given the opkg (IPK format) package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2345
msgid ""
":ref:`populate_sdk_ext <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`: Supports extensible"
" SDK creation under all package managers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2348
msgid ""
"The :ref:`populate_sdk_base <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>` class inherits "
"the appropriate ``populate_sdk_*`` (i.e. ``deb``, ``rpm``, and ``ipk``) "
"based on :term:`IMAGE_PKGTYPE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2352
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The base class ensures all source and destination directories are "
"established and then populates the SDK. After populating the SDK, the "
":ref:`populate_sdk_base <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>` class constructs "
"two sysroots: ``${``\\ :term:`SDK_ARCH`\\ ``}-nativesdk``, which contains"
" the cross-compiler and associated tooling, and the target, which "
"contains a target root filesystem that is configured for the SDK usage. "
"These two images reside in :term:`SDK_OUTPUT`, which consists of the "
"following::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2364
msgid ""
"Finally, the base populate SDK class creates the toolchain environment "
"setup script, the tarball of the SDK, and the installer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2367
msgid ""
"The respective :ref:`populate_sdk_deb <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`, "
":ref:`populate_sdk_rpm <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>`, and "
":ref:`populate_sdk_ipk <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>` classes each support"
" the specific type of SDK. These classes are inherited by and used with "
"the :ref:`populate_sdk_base <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2372
msgid ""
"For more information on the cross-development toolchain generation, see "
"the \":ref:`overview-manual/concepts:cross-development toolchain "
"generation`\" section in the Yocto Project Overview and Concepts Manual. "
"For information on advantages gained when building a cross-development "
"toolchain using the :ref:`ref-tasks-populate_sdk` task, see the \":ref"
":`sdk-manual/appendix-obtain:building an sdk installer`\" section in the "
"Yocto Project Application Development and the Extensible Software "
"Development Kit (eSDK) manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2385
msgid "``prexport``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2387
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-prexport` class provides functionality for "
"exporting :term:`PR` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2392
msgid ""
"This class is not intended to be used directly. Rather, it is enabled "
"when using \"``bitbake-prserv-tool export``\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2398
msgid "``primport``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2400
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-primport` class provides functionality for "
"importing :term:`PR` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2405
msgid ""
"This class is not intended to be used directly. Rather, it is enabled "
"when using \"``bitbake-prserv-tool import``\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2411
msgid "``prserv``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2413
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-prserv` class provides functionality for using a "
":ref:`PR service <dev-manual/packages:working with a pr service>` in "
"order to automatically manage the incrementing of the :term:`PR` variable"
" for each recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2418
msgid ""
"This class is enabled by default because it is inherited by the :ref"
":`ref-classes-package` class. However, the OpenEmbedded build system will"
" not enable the functionality of this class unless :term:`PRSERV_HOST` "
"has been set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2426
msgid "``ptest``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2428
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-ptest` class provides functionality for packaging "
"and installing runtime tests for recipes that build software that "
"provides these tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2431
msgid ""
"This class is intended to be inherited by individual recipes. However, "
"the class' functionality is largely disabled unless \"ptest\" appears in "
":term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`. See the \":ref:`test-manual/ptest:testing "
"packages with ptest`\" section in the Yocto Project Test Environment "
"Manual for more information on ptest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2441
msgid "``ptest-cargo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2443
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-ptest-cargo` class is a class which extends the "
":ref:`ref-classes-cargo` class and adds ``compile_ptest_cargo`` and "
"``install_ptest_cargo`` steps to respectively build and install test "
"suites defined in the ``Cargo.toml`` file, into a dedicated ``-ptest`` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2452
msgid "``ptest-gnome``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2454
msgid ""
"Enables package tests (ptests) specifically for GNOME packages, which "
"have tests intended to be executed with ``gnome-desktop-testing``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2457
msgid ""
"For information on setting up and running ptests, see the \":ref:`test-"
"manual/ptest:testing packages with ptest`\" section in the Yocto Project "
"Test Environment Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2464
msgid "``ptest-python-pytest``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2466
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-ptest-python-pytest` class can be inherited in "
"Python-based recipes to automatically configure the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"ptest` class for Python packages leveraging the `pytest "
"<https://docs.pytest.org>`__ unit test framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2470
msgid ""
"Within the recipe, the :term:`PTEST_PYTEST_DIR` variable specifies the "
"path to the directory containing the tests that will be installed in "
":term:`D` by the :ref:`ref-tasks-install_ptest_base` task, as well as a "
"specific ``run-ptest`` script for this task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2478
msgid "``python3-dir``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2480
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python3-dir` class provides the base version, "
"location, and site package location for Python 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2486
msgid "``python3native``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2488
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python3native` class supports using the native "
"version of Python 3 built by the build system rather than support of the "
"version provided by the build host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2495
msgid "``python3targetconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2497
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-python3targetconfig` class supports using the "
"native version of Python 3 built by the build system rather than support "
"of the version provided by the build host, except that the configuration "
"for the target machine is accessible (such as correct installation "
"directories). This also adds a dependency on target ``python3``, so "
"should only be used where appropriate in order to avoid unnecessarily "
"lengthening builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2507
msgid "``qemu``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2509
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-qemu` class provides functionality for recipes that"
" either need QEMU or test for the existence of QEMU. Typically, this "
"class is used to run programs for a target system on the build host using"
" QEMU's application emulation mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2517
msgid "``recipe_sanity``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2519
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-recipe_sanity` class checks for the presence of any"
" host system recipe prerequisites that might affect the build (e.g. "
"variables that are set or software that is present)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2526
msgid "``relative_symlinks``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2528
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-relative_symlinks` class walks the symbolic links "
"in the :term:`D` directory and replaces links pointing to absolute paths "
"to relative paths. This is occasionally used in some recipes that create "
"wrong symbolic links when their :ref:`ref-classes-native` version is "
"built, and/or would cause breakage in the :ref:`overview-"
"manual/concepts:shared state cache`."
msgstr ""

