#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2538
msgid "It is replaced by::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2545
msgid "``relocatable``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2547
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-relocatable` class enables relocation of binaries "
"when they are installed into the sysroot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2550
msgid ""
"This class makes use of the :ref:`ref-classes-chrpath` class and is used "
"by both the :ref:`ref-classes-cross` and :ref:`ref-classes-native` "
"classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2556
msgid "``remove-libtool``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2558
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-remove-libtool` class adds a post function to the "
":ref:`ref-tasks-install` task to remove all ``.la`` files installed by "
"``libtool``. Removing these files results in them being absent from both "
"the sysroot and target packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2563
msgid ""
"If a recipe needs the ``.la`` files to be installed, then the recipe can "
"override the removal by setting ``REMOVE_LIBTOOL_LA`` to \"0\" as "
"follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2570
msgid "The :ref:`ref-classes-remove-libtool` class is not enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2575
msgid "``report-error``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2577
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-report-error` class supports enabling the "
":ref:`error reporting tool <dev-manual/error-reporting-tool:using the "
"error reporting tool>`\", which allows you to submit build error "
"information to a central database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2581
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The class collects debug information for recipe, recipe version, task, "
"machine, distro, build system, target system, host distro, branch, "
"commit, and log. From the information, report files using a JSON format "
"are created and stored in ``${``\\ :term:`LOG_DIR`\\ ``}/error-report``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2590
msgid "``retain``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2592
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-retain` class can be used to create a tarball of "
"the work directory for a recipe when one of its tasks fails, or any other"
" nominated directories. It is useful in cases where the environment in "
"which builds are run is ephemeral or otherwise inaccessible for "
"examination during debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2597
msgid "To enable, add the following to your configuration::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2601
msgid ""
"The class can be disabled for specific recipes using the "
":term:`RETAIN_ENABLED` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2607
msgid "``rm_work``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2609
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-rm-work` class supports deletion of temporary "
"workspace, which can ease your hard drive demands during builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2612
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The OpenEmbedded build system can use a substantial amount of disk space "
"during the build process. A portion of this space is the work files under"
" the ``${TMPDIR}/work`` directory for each recipe. Once the build system "
"generates the packages for a recipe, the work files for that recipe are "
"no longer needed. However, by default, the build system preserves these "
"files for inspection and possible debugging purposes. If you would rather"
" have these files deleted to save disk space as the build progresses, you"
" can enable :ref:`ref-classes-rm-work` by adding the following to your "
":ref:`structure-build-conf-local.conf` file, which is found in the "
":term:`Build Directory`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2625
msgid ""
"If you are modifying and building source code out of the work directory "
"for a recipe, enabling :ref:`ref-classes-rm-work` will potentially result"
" in your changes to the source being lost. To exclude some recipes from "
"having their work directories deleted by :ref:`ref-classes-rm-work`, you "
"can add the names of the recipe or recipes you are working on to the "
":term:`RM_WORK_EXCLUDE` variable, which can also be set in your :ref"
":`structure-build-conf-local.conf` file. Here is an example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2635
msgid ""
"Finally, if you are using this class for a recipe but want to prevent "
":term:`BitBake` from deleting specific folders or files in that recipe's "
":term:`WORKDIR` (other than ``temp``), you can preserve those folders or "
"files with the :term:`RM_WORK_EXCLUDE_ITEMS` variable as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2645
msgid "``rootfs*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2647
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-rootfs*` classes support creating the root "
"filesystem for an image and consist of the following classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2650
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rootfs-postcommands <ref-classes-rootfs*>` class, which defines"
" filesystem post-processing functions for image recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2653
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rootfs_deb <ref-classes-rootfs*>` class, which supports "
"creation of root filesystems for images built using ``.deb`` packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2656
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rootfs_rpm <ref-classes-rootfs*>` class, which supports "
"creation of root filesystems for images built using ``.rpm`` packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2659
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rootfs_ipk <ref-classes-rootfs*>` class, which supports "
"creation of root filesystems for images built using ``.ipk`` packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2662
msgid ""
"The :ref:`rootfsdebugfiles <ref-classes-rootfs*>` class, which installs "
"additional files found on the build host directly into the root "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2665
msgid ""
"The root filesystem is created from packages using one of the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-rootfs*` files as determined by the :term:`PACKAGE_CLASSES` "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2669
msgid ""
"For information on how root filesystem images are created, see the \":ref"
":`overview-manual/concepts:image generation`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Overview and Concepts Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2676
msgid "``rust``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2678
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-rust` class is an internal class which is just used"
" in the \"rust\" recipe, to build the Rust compiler and runtime library. "
"Except for this recipe, it is not intended to be used directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2685
msgid "``rust-common``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2687
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-rust-common` class is an internal class to the :ref"
":`ref-classes-cargo_common` and :ref:`ref-classes-rust` classes and is "
"not intended to be used directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2694
msgid "``rust-target-config``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2696
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-rust-target-config` class is an internal class to "
"the :ref:`ref-classes-cargo_common` and :ref:`ref-classes-rust` classes "
"and is not intended to be used directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2700
msgid ""
"It is used to generate a JSON specification file from the features listed"
" in :term:`TUNE_FEATURES`, which is used for cross-compiling. The logic "
"is done in a ``do_rust_gen_targets`` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2707
msgid "``sanity``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2709
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-sanity` class checks to see if prerequisite "
"software is present on the host system so that users can be notified of "
"potential problems that might affect their build. The class also performs"
" basic user configuration checks from the :ref:`structure-build-conf-"
"local.conf` configuration file to prevent common mistakes that cause "
"build failures. Distribution policy usually determines whether to include"
" this class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2719
msgid "``sbom-cve-check``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2721
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-sbom-cve-check` class uses the `sbom-cve-check "
"<https://github.com/bootlin/sbom-cve-check>`__ command-line tool for "
"post-build CVE analysis. It relies on the :ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx` "
"class as SPDX files are the input of this tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2726
msgid ""
"This class should be enabled through the :ref:`ref-fragments-core-yocto-"
"sbom-cve-check` fragment:"
