"The :ref:`ref-classes-python_setuptools_build_meta` class enables "
"building Python modules which declare the `PEP-517 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0517/>`__ compliant "
"``setuptools.build_meta`` ``build-backend`` in the ``[build-system]`` "
"section of ``pyproject.toml`` (See `PEP-518 "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0518/>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2800
msgid ""
"Python modules built with ``setuptools.build_meta`` can be pure Python or"
" include ``C`` or ``Rust`` extensions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2808
msgid "``setuptools3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2810
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` class supports Python version 3.x "
"extensions that use build systems based on ``setuptools`` (e.g. only have"
" a ``setup.py`` and have not migrated to the official ``pyproject.toml`` "
"format). If your recipe uses these build systems, the recipe needs to "
"inherit the :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2818
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` class :ref:`ref-tasks-compile` task "
"now calls ``setup.py bdist_wheel`` to build the ``wheel`` binary archive "
"format (See `PEP-427 <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0427/>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2822
msgid ""
"A consequence of this is that legacy software still using deprecated "
"``distutils`` from the Python standard library cannot be packaged as "
"``wheels``. A common solution is the replace ``from distutils.core import"
" setup`` with ``from setuptools import setup``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2829
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` class :ref:`ref-tasks-install` task "
"now installs the ``wheel`` binary archive. In current versions of "
"``setuptools`` the legacy ``setup.py install`` method is deprecated. If "
"the ``setup.py`` cannot be used with wheels, for example it creates files"
" outside of the Python module or standard entry points, then :ref:`ref-"
"classes-setuptools3_legacy` should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2839
msgid "``setuptools3_legacy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2841
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3_legacy` class supports Python version "
"3.x extensions that use build systems based on ``setuptools`` (e.g. only "
"have a ``setup.py`` and have not migrated to the official "
"``pyproject.toml`` format). Unlike :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3`, this "
"uses the traditional ``setup.py`` ``build`` and ``install`` commands and "
"not wheels. This use of ``setuptools`` like this is `deprecated "
"<https://github.com/pypa/setuptools/blob/14cc4452199818e60cf01cd9cea96e90761abce7/NEWS.rst#v5830>`__"
" but still relatively common."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2853
msgid "``setuptools3-base``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2855
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3-base` class provides a reusable base "
"for other classes that support building Python version 3.x extensions. If"
" you need functionality that is not provided by the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"setuptools3` class, you may want to ``inherit setuptools3-base``. Some "
"recipes do not need the tasks in the :ref:`ref-classes-setuptools3` class"
" and inherit this class instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2864
msgid "``sign_rpm``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2866
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-sign_rpm` class supports generating signed RPM "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2871
msgid "``siteinfo``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2873
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-siteinfo` class provides information about the "
"targets that might be needed by other classes or recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2876
msgid ""
"As an example, consider Autotools, which can require tests that must "
"execute on the target hardware. Since this is not possible in general "
"when cross compiling, site information is used to provide cached test "
"results so these tests can be skipped over but still make the correct "
"values available. The ``meta/site directory`` contains test results "
"sorted into different categories such as architecture, endianness, and "
"the ``libc`` used. Site information provides a list of files containing "
"data relevant to the current build in the :term:`CONFIG_SITE` variable "
"that Autotools automatically picks up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2886
msgid ""
"The class also provides variables like :term:`SITEINFO_ENDIANNESS` and "
":term:`SITEINFO_BITS` that can be used elsewhere in the metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2892
msgid "``sstate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2894
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-sstate` class provides support for Shared State "
"(sstate). By default, the class is enabled through the "
":term:`INHERIT_DISTRO` variable's default value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2898
msgid ""
"For more information on sstate, see the \":ref:`overview-"
"manual/concepts:shared state cache`\" section in the Yocto Project "
"Overview and Concepts Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2905
msgid "``staging``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2907
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-staging` class installs files into individual "
"recipe work directories for sysroots. The class contains the following "
"key tasks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2910
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-tasks-populate_sysroot` task, which is responsible for "
"handing the files that end up in the recipe sysroots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2914
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-tasks-prepare_recipe_sysroot` task (a \"partner\" task to "
"the ``populate_sysroot`` task), which installs the files into the "
"individual recipe work directories (i.e. :term:`WORKDIR`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2920
msgid ""
"The code in the :ref:`ref-classes-staging` class is complex and basically"
" works in two stages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2923
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"*Stage One:* The first stage addresses recipes that have files they want "
"to share with other recipes that have dependencies on the originating "
"recipe. Normally these dependencies are installed through the :ref:`ref-"
"tasks-install` task into ``${``\\ :term:`D`\\ ``}``. The :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"populate_sysroot` task copies a subset of these files into "
"``${SYSROOT_DESTDIR}``. This subset of files is controlled by the "
":term:`SYSROOT_DIRS`, :term:`SYSROOT_DIRS_NATIVE`, and "
":term:`SYSROOT_DIRS_IGNORE` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2937
msgid ""
"Additionally, a recipe can customize the files further by declaring a "
"processing function in the :term:`SYSROOT_PREPROCESS_FUNCS` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2941
msgid ""
"A shared state (sstate) object is built from these files and the files "
"are placed into a subdirectory of :ref:`structure-build-tmp-sysroots-"
"components`. The files are scanned for hardcoded paths to the original "
"installation location. If the location is found in text files, the "
"hardcoded locations are replaced by tokens and a list of the files "
"needing such replacements is created. These adjustments are referred to "
"as \"FIXMEs\". The list of files that are scanned for paths is controlled"
" by the :term:`SSTATE_SCAN_FILES` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2952
msgid ""
"*Stage Two:* The second stage addresses recipes that want to use "
"something from another recipe and declare a dependency on that recipe "
"through the :term:`DEPENDS` variable. The recipe will have a :ref:`ref-"
"tasks-prepare_recipe_sysroot` task and when this task executes, it "
"creates the ``recipe-sysroot`` and ``recipe-sysroot-native`` in the "
"recipe work directory (i.e. :term:`WORKDIR`). The OpenEmbedded build "
"system creates hard links to copies of the relevant files from "
"``sysroots-components`` into the recipe work directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2965
msgid "If hard links are not possible, the build system uses actual copies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2968
msgid ""
"The build system then addresses any \"FIXMEs\" to paths as defined from "
"the list created in the first stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2971
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Finally, any files in ``${bindir}`` within the sysroot that have the "
"prefix \"``postinst-``\" are executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2976
msgid ""
"Although such sysroot post installation scripts are not recommended for "
"general use, the files do allow some issues such as user creation and "
"module indexes to be addressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2980
msgid ""
"Because recipes can have other dependencies outside of :term:`DEPENDS` "
"(e.g. ``do_unpack[depends] += \"tar-native:do_populate_sysroot\"``), the "
"sysroot creation function ``extend_recipe_sysroot`` is also added as a "
"pre-function for those tasks whose dependencies are not through "
":term:`DEPENDS` but operate similarly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2986
msgid ""
"When installing dependencies into the sysroot, the code traverses the "
"dependency graph and processes dependencies in exactly the same way as "
"the dependencies would or would not be when installed from sstate. This "
"processing means, for example, a native tool would have its native "
"dependencies added but a target library would not have its dependencies "
"traversed or installed. The same sstate dependency code is used so that "
"builds should be identical regardless of whether sstate was used or not. "
"For a closer look, see the ``setscene_depvalid()`` function in the :ref"
":`ref-classes-sstate` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:2996
msgid ""
"The build system is careful to maintain manifests of the files it "
"installs so that any given dependency can be installed as needed. The "
"sstate hash of the installed item is also stored so that if it changes, "
"the build system can reinstall it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3004
msgid "``syslinux``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3006
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-syslinux` class provides syslinux-specific "
"functions for building bootable images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3009
msgid "The class supports the following variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3011
msgid ""
":term:`INITRD`: Indicates list of filesystem images to concatenate and "
"use as an initial RAM disk (initrd). This variable is optional."
