msgid ""
"Services are set up to start on boot automatically unless you have set "
":term:`SYSTEMD_AUTO_ENABLE` to \"disable\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3075
msgid ""
"For more information on :ref:`ref-classes-systemd`, see the \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/init-manager:selecting an initialization manager`\" section in the"
" Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3082
msgid "``systemd-boot``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3084
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-systemd-boot` class provides functions specific to "
"the systemd-boot bootloader for building bootable images. This is an "
"internal class and is not intended to be used directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3090
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-systemd-boot` class is a result from merging the "
"``gummiboot`` class used in previous Yocto Project releases with the "
"``systemd`` project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3093
msgid ""
"Set the :term:`EFI_PROVIDER` variable to \":ref:`ref-classes-systemd-"
"boot`\" to use this class. Doing so creates a standalone EFI bootloader "
"that is not dependent on systemd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3097
msgid ""
"For information on more variables used and supported in this class, see "
"the :term:`SYSTEMD_BOOT_CFG`, :term:`SYSTEMD_BOOT_ENTRIES`, and "
":term:`SYSTEMD_BOOT_TIMEOUT` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3102
msgid ""
"You can also see the `Systemd-boot documentation "
"<https://systemd.io/BOOT/>`__ for more information."
