msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-waf` class supports recipes that need to build "
"software that uses the Waf build system. You can use the "
":term:`EXTRA_OECONF` or :term:`PACKAGECONFIG_CONFARGS` variables to "
"specify additional configuration options to be passed on the Waf command "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3884
msgid "``yocto-check-layer``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3886
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ref-classes-yocto-check-layer` class is used by the :oe_git"
":`yocto-check-layer </openembedded-core/tree/scripts/yocto-check-layer>` "
"script to ensure that packages from Yocto Project Compatible layers don't"
" skip required QA checks listed in :term:`CHECKLAYER_REQUIRED_TESTS` "
"defined by the :ref:`ref-classes-insane` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3892
msgid ""
"It adds an anonymous python function with extra processing to all "
"recipes, and globally inheriting this class with :term:`INHERIT` is not "
"advised. Instead the ``yocto-check-layer`` script should be used as it "
"handles usage of this class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/classes.rst:3897
msgid ""
"For more information on the Yocto Project Compatible layers, see the :ref"
":`dev-manual/layers:Making Sure Your Layer is Compatible With Yocto "
"Project` section of the Yocto Project Development Manual."
msgstr ""

