msgid "Creating the Workspace Layer in an Alternative Location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:602
msgid ""
"Use the ``devtool create-workspace`` command to create a new workspace "
"layer in your :term:`Build Directory`. When you create a new workspace "
"layer, it is populated with the ``README`` file and the ``conf`` "
"directory only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:607
msgid ""
"The following example creates a new workspace layer in your current "
"working and by default names the workspace layer \"workspace\"::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:612
msgid ""
"You can create a workspace layer anywhere by supplying a pathname with "
"the command. The following command creates a new workspace layer named "
"\"new-workspace\"::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:621
msgid "Get the Status of the Recipes in Your Workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:623
msgid ""
"Use the ``devtool status`` command to list the recipes currently in your "
"workspace. Information includes the paths to their respective external "
"source trees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:627
msgid "The ``devtool status`` command has no command-line options::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:631
msgid ""
"Here is sample output after using :ref:`devtool add <ref-manual/devtool-"
"reference:adding a new recipe to the workspace layer>` to create and add "
"the ``mtr_0.86.bb`` recipe to the ``workspace`` directory::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:642
msgid "Search for Available Target Recipes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:644
msgid ""
"Use the ``devtool search`` command to search for available target "
"recipes. The command matches the recipe name, package name, description, "
"and installed files. The command displays the recipe name as a result of "
"a match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:649
msgid ""
"When you use the ``devtool search`` command, you must supply a keyword. "
"The command uses the keyword when searching for a match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:652
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the ``devtool find-recipe`` command can be used to search "
"for recipe files instead of recipe names. Likewise, you must supply a "
"keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:658
msgid "Get Information on Recipe Configuration Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:660
msgid ""
"Use the ``devtool configure-help`` command to get help on the "
"configuration script options for a given recipe. You must supply the "
"recipe name to the command. For example, it shows the output of "
"``./configure --help`` for :ref:`autotools <ref-classes-autotools>`-based"
" recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:665
msgid ""
"The ``configure-help`` command will also display the configuration "
"options currently in use, including the ones passed through the "
":term:`EXTRA_OECONF` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:672
msgid "Generate an IDE Configuration for a Recipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:674
msgid ""
"The ``devtool ide-sdk`` automatically creates an IDE configuration and "
"SDK to work on a given recipe. Depending on the ``--mode`` parameter, "
"different types of SDKs are generated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:678
msgid ""
"``modified`` mode: this creates an SDK and generates an IDE configuration"
" in the workspace directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:681
msgid ""
"``shared`` mode: this creates a cross-compiling toolchain and the "
"corresponding shared sysroot directories of the supplied recipe(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:684
msgid ""
"The ``--target`` option can be used to specify a ``username@hostname`` "
"string and create a remote debugging configuration for the recipe. "
"Similarly to ``devtool deploy-target``, it requires an SSH server running"
" on the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/devtool-reference.rst:688
msgid ""
"For further details on the ``devtool ide-sdk`` command, see the \":doc"
":`/sdk-manual/extensible`\" chapter in the Yocto Project Application "
"Development and the Extensible Software Development Kit (eSDK) manual."
msgstr ""

