#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:137
msgid "Another option is to set::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:141
msgid ""
"This statement tells BitBake to issue an error instead of trying to "
"access the Internet. This technique is useful if you want to ensure code "
"builds only from local sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:145
msgid "Here is another technique::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:149
msgid ""
"This statement limits the build system to pulling source from the "
":term:`PREMIRRORS` only.  Again, this technique is useful for reproducing"
" builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:153
msgid "Here is yet another technique::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:157
msgid ""
"This statement tells the build system to generate mirror tarballs. This "
"technique is useful if you want to create a mirror server. If not, "
"however, the technique can simply waste time during the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:161
msgid ""
"Finally, consider an example where you are behind an HTTP-only firewall. "
"You could make the following changes to a :term:`configuration file` as "
"long as the :term:`PREMIRRORS` server is current::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:173
msgid ""
"These changes would cause the build system to successfully fetch source "
"over HTTP and any network accesses to anything other than the "
":term:`PREMIRRORS` would fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:177
msgid ""
"Most source fetching by the OpenEmbedded build system is done by ``wget``"
" and you therefore need to specify the proxy settings in a ``.wgetrc`` "
"file, which can be in your home directory if you are a single user or can"
" be in ``/usr/local/etc/wgetrc`` as a global user file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/faq.rst:183
msgid ""
"Here is the applicable code for setting various proxy types in the "
"``.wgetrc`` file. By default, these settings are disabled with comments. "
"To use them, remove the comments::"
