#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:273
msgid "Image Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:275
msgid ""
"The contents of images generated by the OpenEmbedded build system can be "
"controlled by the :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` and :term:`EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES`"
" variables that you typically configure in your image recipes. Through "
"these variables, you can add several different predefined packages such "
"as development utilities or packages with debug information needed to "
"investigate application problems or profile applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:283
msgid "The image features available for all images are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:285
msgid ""
"*allow-empty-password:* Allows Dropbear and OpenSSH to accept logins from"
" accounts having an empty password string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:288
msgid "*allow-root-login:* Allows Dropbear and OpenSSH to accept root logins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:290
msgid ""
"*dbg-pkgs:* Installs debug symbol packages for all packages installed in "
"a given image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:293
msgid ""
"*dev-pkgs:* Installs development packages (headers and extra library "
"links) for all packages installed in a given image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:296
msgid ""
"*doc-pkgs:* Installs documentation packages for all packages installed in"
" a given image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:299
msgid ""
"*empty-root-password:* This feature can be used if you want to allow root"
" login with an empty password. If this feature is not present in "
":term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`, a non-empty password is forced in ``/etc/passwd``"
" and ``/etc/shadow`` if such files exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:305
msgid ""
"``empty-root-password`` doesn't set an empty root password by itself. You"
" get an initial empty root password thanks to the :oe_git:`base-passwd "
"</openembedded-core/tree/meta/recipes-core/base-passwd/>` and "
":oe_git:`shadow </openembedded-core/tree/meta/recipes-extended/shadow/>` "
"recipes, and the presence of ``empty-root-password`` just disables the "
"mechanism which forces an non-empty password for the root user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:312
msgid ""
"*lic-pkgs:* Installs license packages for all packages installed in a "
"given image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:315
msgid ""
"*overlayfs-etc:* Configures the ``/etc`` directory to be in "
"``overlayfs``. This allows to store device specific information "
"elsewhere, especially if the root filesystem is configured to be read-"
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:319
msgid ""
"*package-management:* Installs package management tools and preserves the"
" package manager database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:322
msgid ""
"*post-install-logging:* Enables logging postinstall script runs to the "
"``/var/log/postinstall.log`` file on first boot of the image on the "
"target system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:328
msgid ""
"To make the ``/var/log`` directory on the target persistent, remove the "
"``files/fs-perms-volatile-log.txt`` value from "
":term:`FILESYSTEM_PERMS_TABLES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:332
msgid "*ptest-pkgs:* Installs ptest packages for all ptest-enabled recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:334
msgid ""
"*read-only-rootfs:* Creates an image whose root filesystem is read-only. "
"See the \":ref:`security-manual/read-only-rootfs:creating a read-only "
"root filesystem`\" section in the Yocto Project Security Manual for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:340
msgid ""
"*read-only-rootfs-delayed-postinsts:* when specified in conjunction with "
"``read-only-rootfs``, specifies that post-install scripts are still "
"permitted (this assumes that the root filesystem will be made writeable "
"for the first boot; this feature does not do anything to ensure that - it"
" just disables the check for post-install scripts.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:346
msgid ""
"*serial-autologin-root:* when specified in conjunction with ``empty-root-"
"password`` will automatically login as root on the serial console. This "
"of course opens up a security hole if the serial console is potentially "
"accessible to an attacker, so use with caution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:352
msgid ""
"*splash:* Enables showing a splash screen during boot. By default, this "
"screen is provided by ``psplash``, which does allow customization. If you"
" prefer to use an alternative splash screen package, you can do so by "
"setting the :term:`SPLASH` variable to a different package name (or "
"names) within the image recipe or at the distro configuration level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:359
msgid ""
"*stateless-rootfs:* specifies that the image should be created as "
"stateless - when using ``systemd``, ``systemctl-native`` will not be run "
"on the image, leaving the image for population at runtime by systemd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:364
msgid ""
"*staticdev-pkgs:* Installs static development packages, which are static "
"libraries (i.e. ``*.a`` files), for all packages installed in a given "
"image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:368
msgid ""
"Some image features are available only when you inherit the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-core-image` class. The current list of these valid features is as"
" follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:372
msgid "*hwcodecs:* Installs hardware acceleration codecs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:374
msgid "*nfs-server:* Installs an NFS server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:376
msgid ""
"*perf:* Installs profiling tools such as ``perf``, ``systemtap``, and "
"``LTTng``. For general information on user-space tools, see the :doc"
":`/sdk-manual/index` manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:380
msgid "*ssh-server-dropbear:* Installs the Dropbear minimal SSH server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:384
msgid ""
"As of the 4.1 release, the ``ssh-server-dropbear`` feature also "
"recommends the ``openssh-sftp-server`` package, which by default will be "
"pulled into the image. This is because recent versions of the OpenSSH "
"``scp`` client now use the SFTP protocol, and thus require an SFTP server"
" to be present to connect to. However, if you wish to use the Dropbear "
"ssh server `without` the SFTP server installed, you can either remove "
"``ssh-server-dropbear`` from ``IMAGE_FEATURES`` and add ``dropbear`` to "
":term:`IMAGE_INSTALL` instead, or alternatively still use the feature but"
" set :term:`BAD_RECOMMENDATIONS` as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:397
msgid ""
"*ssh-server-openssh:* Installs the OpenSSH SSH server, which is more "
"full-featured than Dropbear. Note that if both the OpenSSH SSH server and"
" the Dropbear minimal SSH server are present in :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`, "
"then OpenSSH will take precedence and Dropbear will not be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:403
msgid ""
"*tools-debug:* Installs debugging tools such as ``strace`` and ``gdb``. "
"For information on GDB, see the \":ref:`dev-manual/debugging:debugging "
"with the gnu project debugger (gdb) remotely`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual. For information on tracing and "
"profiling, see the :doc:`/profile-manual/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:409
msgid ""
"*tools-profile:*: Installs profiling tools such as ``perf``. See the :ref"
":`profile-manual/intro:Yocto Project Profiling and Tracing Manual` for "
"more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:413
msgid "*tools-sdk:* Installs a full SDK that runs on the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:415
msgid ""
"*tools-testapps:* Installs device testing tools (e.g. touchscreen "
"debugging)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:418
msgid "*weston:* Installs Weston (reference Wayland environment)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:420
msgid "*x11:* Installs the X server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:422
msgid "*x11-base:* Installs the X server with a minimal environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:424
msgid "*x11-sato:* Installs the OpenedHand Sato environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:430
msgid "SDK Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/features.rst:432
msgid ""
"The contents of a :ref:`standard <sdk-manual/using:Using the Standard "
"SDK>` or :ref:`extensible <sdk-manual/extensible:Using the extensible "
"SDK>` SDK generated by the :term:`OpenEmbedded Build System` can be "
"controlled by the :term:`SDK_FEATURES` variable that you typically "
"configure in the image recipe for which the :ref:`ref-tasks-populate_sdk`"
" or :ref:`ref-tasks-populate_sdk_ext` task is run."
