msgid "Core Configuration Fragments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:177
msgid "Yocto Project Fragments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:179
msgid ""
"This group defines fragments related to the Yocto Project infrastructure "
"in general."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:185
msgid "``core/yocto/sstate-mirror-cdn``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:187
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto/sstate-mirror-cdn`` :term:`configuration fragment` can "
"be used to set up :term:`BB_HASHSERVE_UPSTREAM` and "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` to use pre-built :ref:`shared state cache "
"<overview-manual/concepts:shared state cache>` artifacts for standard "
"Yocto build configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:192
msgid ""
"This will mean the build will query the Yocto Project mirrors to check "
"for artifacts at the start of builds, which does slow it down initially "
"but it will then speed up the builds by not having to build things if "
"they are present in the cache. It assumes you can download something "
"faster than you can build it which will depend on your network "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:201
msgid "``core/yocto/root-login-with-empty-password``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:203
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto/root-login-with-empty-password`` :term:`configuration "
"fragment` can be used to allow to login as the ``root`` user to login "
"without a password on the serial console and over SSH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:210
msgid "``core/yocto/sbom-cve-check``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:212
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto/sbom-cve-check`` :term:`configuration fragment` can be "
"used to set up the build to use the :ref:`ref-classes-sbom-cve-check` "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:215
msgid "This configuration fragment does multiple things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:217
msgid ""
"Adds the :ref:`ref-classes-create-spdx` class to the list of globally "
"inherited classes, as it depends on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:220
msgid ""
"Sets the source revision (:term:`SRCREV`) of the input CVE databases to "
":term:`AUTOREV`, so these databases are automatically fetched and updated"
" when starting a build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:224
msgid ""
"Includes the VEX statements to the input SPDX document using the "
":term:`SPDX_INCLUDE_VEX` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:230
msgid "``core/yocto/monitor-disk-space``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:232
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto/monitor-disk-space`` :term:`configuration fragment` can "
"be used to produce warnings or errors when the disk currently in use "
"during the build is out of space, by setting a sensible value for the "
":term:`BB_DISKMON_DIRS` variable. See the definition of "
":term:`BB_DISKMON_DIRS` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:238
msgid "Yocto Project Autobuilder Fragments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:240
msgid ""
"This group defines fragment used for the Yocto Project Autobuilder. For "
"details, see the :ref:`test-manual/intro:Yocto Project Autobuilder "
"Overview` section of the Yocto Project Test Environment Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:247
msgid "``core/yocto-autobuilder/autobuilder``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:249
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto-autobuilder/autobuilder`` fragment defines common "
"variables used in builds started by the Yocto Project Autobuilder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:255
msgid "``core/yocto-autobuilder/autobuilder-resource-constraints``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:257
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto-autobuilder/autobuilder`` fragment defines variables for"
" limiting the resources used by the Yocto Project Autobuilder during "
"builds. For more details on how to limit resources, see the :doc:`/dev-"
"manual/limiting-resources` section of the Yocto Project Development Tasks"
" Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:265
msgid "``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-mips64-n32``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:267
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-mips64-n32`` fragment enables tri-"
"architecture :ref:`multilib <dev-manual/libraries:Combining Multiple "
"Versions of Library Files into One Image>` configurations for "
":wikipedia:`MIPS64 <MIPS_architecture>` machines, which includes "
"``mips64-n32``, ``mips64``, and ``mips32r2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:276
msgid "``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-x86-lib32``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:278
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-x86-lib32`` fragment enables "
":ref:`multilib <dev-manual/libraries:Combining Multiple Versions of "
"Library Files into One Image>` configurations for supporting 32-bit "
"libraries on 64-bit :wikipedia:`X86 <X86>` builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:286
msgid "``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-x86-lib64``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/fragments.rst:288
msgid ""
"The ``core/yocto-autobuilder/multilib-x86-lib64`` fragment enables "
":ref:`multilib <dev-manual/libraries:Combining Multiple Versions of "
"Library Files into One Image>` configurations for supporting 64-bit "
"libraries on 32-bit :wikipedia:`X86 <X86>` builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:5
msgid "Images"
msgstr "Immagini"

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:7
msgid ""
"The OpenEmbedded build system provides several example images to satisfy "
"different needs. When you issue the ``bitbake`` command you provide a "
"\"top-level\" recipe that essentially begins the build for the type of "
"image you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:14
msgid ""
"Building an image without GNU General Public License Version 3 (GPLv3), "
"GNU Lesser General Public License Version 3 (LGPLv3), and the GNU Affero "
"General Public License Version 3 (AGPL-3.0) components is only tested for"
" core-image-minimal image. Furthermore, if you would like to build an "
"image and verify that it does not include GPLv3 and similarly licensed "
"components, you must make the following changes in the image recipe file "
"before using the BitBake command to build the image:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:22
msgid "INCOMPATIBLE_LICENSE = \"GPL-3.0* LGPL-3.0*\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:24
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can adjust your distro :term:`configuration file`, "
"repeating and adjusting the line for all images where the license "
"restriction must apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:28
msgid "INCOMPATIBLE_LICENSE:pn-your-image-name = \"GPL-3.0* LGPL-3.0*\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:30
msgid ""
"From within the :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core (OE-Core)` Git repository, you "
"can use the following command to display the list of directories that "
"contain image recipe files::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:35
msgid "Here is a list of supported recipes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:37
msgid ""
"``build-appliance-image``: An example virtual machine that contains all "
"the pieces required to run builds using the build system as well as the "
"build system itself. You can boot and run the image using `VMware "
"Workstation <https://www.vmware.com/products/desktop-hypervisor"
"/workstation-and-fusion>`__. For more information on this image, see the "
":yocto_home:`Build Appliance </software-item/build-appliance>` page on "
"the Yocto Project website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:45
msgid ""
"``core-image-base``: A console-only image that fully supports the target "
"device hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:48
msgid ""
"``core-image-full-cmdline``: A console-only image with more full-featured"
" Linux system functionality installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:51
msgid ""
"``core-image-minimal``: A small image just capable of allowing a device "
"to boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:54
msgid ""
"``core-image-minimal-dev``: A ``core-image-minimal`` image suitable for "
"development work using the host. The image includes headers and libraries"
" you can use in a host development environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:58
msgid ""
"``core-image-minimal-initramfs``: A ``core-image-minimal`` image that has"
" the Minimal RAM-based Initial Root Filesystem (:term:`Initramfs`) as "
"part of the kernel, which allows the system to find the first \"init\" "
"program more efficiently. See the :term:`PACKAGE_INSTALL` variable for "
"additional information helpful when working with :term:`Initramfs` "
"images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:65
msgid ""
"``core-image-minimal-mtdutils``: A ``core-image-minimal`` image that has "
"support for the Minimal MTD Utilities, which let the user interact with "
"the MTD subsystem in the kernel to perform operations on flash devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:70
msgid ""
"``core-image-rt``: A ``core-image-minimal`` image plus a real-time test "
"suite and tools appropriate for real-time use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:73
msgid ""
"``core-image-rt-sdk``: A ``core-image-rt`` image that includes everything"
" in the cross-toolchain. The image also includes development headers and "
"libraries to form a complete stand-alone SDK and is suitable for "
"development using the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:78
msgid ""
"``core-image-sato``: An image with Sato support, a mobile environment and"
" visual style that works well with mobile devices. The image supports X11"
" with a Sato theme and applications such as a terminal, editor, file "
"manager, media player, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:83
msgid ""
"``core-image-sato-dev``: A ``core-image-sato`` image suitable for "
"development using the host. The image includes libraries needed to build "
"applications on the device itself, testing and profiling tools, and debug"
" symbols. This image was formerly ``core-image-sdk``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:88
msgid ""
"``core-image-sato-sdk``: A ``core-image-sato`` image that includes "
"everything in the cross-toolchain. The image also includes development "
"headers and libraries to form a complete standalone SDK and is suitable "
"for development using the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:93
msgid ""
"``core-image-testmaster``: A \"controller\" image designed to be used for"
" automated runtime testing. Provides a \"known good\" image that is "
"deployed to a separate partition so that you can boot into it and use it "
"to deploy a second image to be tested. You can find more information "
"about runtime testing in the \":ref:`test-manual/runtime-"
"testing:performing automated runtime testing`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Test Environment Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:101
msgid ""
"``core-image-testmaster-initramfs``: A RAM-based Initial Root Filesystem "
"(:term:`Initramfs`) image tailored for use with the ``core-image-"
"testmaster`` image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:105
msgid ""
"``core-image-weston``: A very basic Wayland image with a terminal. This "
"image provides the Wayland protocol libraries and the reference Weston "
"compositor. For more information, see the \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/wayland:using wayland and weston`\" section in the Yocto Project "
"Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/images.rst:111
msgid "``core-image-x11``: A very basic X11 image with a terminal."
msgstr ""

