#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:5
msgid "OpenEmbedded Kickstart (``.wks``) Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:10 ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:10
#: ../../ref-manual/resources.rst:10
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduzione"

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:12
msgid ""
"This chapter provides a reference on the available kickstart commands. "
"The information lists the commands, their syntax, and meanings. Kickstart"
" commands are based on the Fedora kickstart versions but with "
"modifications to reflect Wic capabilities. You can see the original "
"documentation for those commands at the following link: "
"https://pykickstart.readthedocs.io/en/latest/kickstart-docs.html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:20
msgid "Command: part or partition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:22
msgid ""
"Either of these commands creates a partition on the system and uses the "
"following syntax::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:28
msgid ""
"If you do not provide mntpoint, Wic creates a partition but does not "
"mount it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:31
msgid ""
"The ``mntpoint`` is where the partition is mounted and must be in one of "
"the following forms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:34
msgid "``/path``: For example, \"/\", \"/usr\", or \"/home\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:36
msgid "``swap``: The created partition is used as swap space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:38
msgid ""
"Specifying a mntpoint causes the partition to automatically be mounted. "
"Wic achieves this by adding entries to the filesystem table (fstab) "
"during image generation. In order for Wic to generate a valid fstab, you "
"must also provide one of the ``--ondrive``, ``--ondisk``, or ``--use-"
"uuid`` partition options as part of the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:46
msgid ""
"The mount program must understand the PARTUUID syntax you use with "
"``--use-uuid`` and non-root *mountpoint*, including swap. The default "
"configuration of BusyBox in OpenEmbedded supports this, but this may be "
"disabled in custom configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:51
msgid ""
"Here is an example that uses \"/\" as the mountpoint. The command uses "
"``--ondisk`` to force the partition onto the ``sdb`` disk::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:56
msgid ""
"Here is a list that describes other supported options you can use with "
"the ``part`` and ``partition`` commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:59
msgid ""
"``--size``: The minimum partition size. Specify as an integer value "
"optionally followed by one of the units \"k\" / \"K\" for kibibyte, \"M\""
" for mebibyte and \"G\" for gibibyte. The default unit if none is given "
"is \"M\". You do not need this option if you use ``--source``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:64
msgid ""
"``--fixed-size``: The exact partition size. Specify as an integer value "
"optionally followed by one of the units \"k\" / \"K\" for kibibyte, \"M\""
" for mebibyte and \"G\" for gibibyte. The default unit if none is given "
"is \"M\".  Cannot be specify together with ``--size``. An error occurs "
"when assembling the disk image if the partition data is larger than "
"``--fixed-size``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:71
msgid ""
"``--source``: This option is a Wic-specific option that names the source "
"of the data that populates the partition. The most common value for this "
"option is \"rootfs\", but you can use any value that maps to a valid "
"source plugin. For information on the source plugins, see the \":ref"
":`dev-manual/wic:using the wic plugin interface`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:78
msgid ""
"If you use ``--source rootfs``, Wic creates a partition as large as "
"needed and fills it with the contents of the root filesystem pointed to "
"by the ``-r`` command-line option or the equivalent root filesystem "
"derived from the ``-e`` command-line option. The filesystem type used to "
"create the partition is driven by the value of the ``--fstype`` option "
"specified for the partition. See the entry on ``--fstype`` that follows "
"for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:86
msgid ""
"If you use ``--source plugin-name``, Wic creates a partition as large as "
"needed and fills it with the contents of the partition that is generated "
"by the specified plugin name using the data pointed to by the ``-r`` "
"command-line option or the equivalent root filesystem derived from the "
"``-e`` command-line option. Exactly what those contents are and "
"filesystem type used are dependent on the given plugin implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:94
msgid ""
"If you do not use the ``--source`` option, the ``wic`` command creates an"
" empty partition. Consequently, you must use the ``--size`` option to "
"specify the size of the empty partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:98
msgid ""
"``--ondisk`` or ``--ondrive``: Forces the partition to be created on a "
"particular disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:101
msgid ""
"``--fstype``: Sets the file system type for the partition. Valid values "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:104
msgid "``btrfs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:106
msgid "``erofs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:108
msgid "``ext2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:110
msgid "``ext3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:112
msgid "``ext4``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:114
msgid "``squashfs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:116
msgid "``swap``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:118
msgid "``vfat``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:120
msgid ""
"``--fsoptions``: Specifies a free-form string of options to be used when "
"mounting the filesystem. This string is copied into the ``/etc/fstab`` "
"file of the installed system and should be enclosed in quotes. If not "
"specified, the default string is \"defaults\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:125
msgid ""
"``--label label``: Specifies the label to give to the filesystem to be "
"made on the partition. If the given label is already in use by another "
"filesystem, a new label is created for the partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:129
msgid "``--active``: Marks the partition as active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:131
msgid ""
"``--align (in KBytes)``: This option is a Wic-specific option that says "
"to start partitions on boundaries given x KBytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:134
msgid ""
"``--offset``: This option is a Wic-specific option that says to place a "
"partition at exactly the specified offset. If the partition cannot be "
"placed at the specified offset, the image build will fail. Specify as an "
"integer value optionally followed by one of the units \"s\" / \"S\" for "
"512 byte sector, \"k\" / \"K\" for kibibyte, \"M\" for mebibyte and \"G\""
" for gibibyte. The default unit if none is given is \"k\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:142
msgid ""
"``--no-table``: This option is a Wic-specific option. Using the option "
"reserves space for the partition and causes it to become populated. "
"However, the partition is not added to the partition table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:147
msgid ""
"``--exclude-path``: This option is a Wic-specific option that excludes "
"the given relative path from the resulting image. This option is only "
"effective with the rootfs source plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:151
msgid ""
"``--extra-filesystem-space``: This option is a Wic-specific option that "
"adds extra space after the space filled by the content of the partition. "
"The final size can exceed the size specified by the ``--size`` option. "
"The default value is 10M. Specify as an integer value optionally followed"
" by one of the units \"k\" / \"K\" for kibibyte, \"M\" for mebibyte and "
"\"G\" for gibibyte. The default unit if none is given is \"M\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:159
msgid ""
"``--extra-partition-space``: This option is a Wic-specific option that "
"adds extra empty space after the space filled by the filesystem. With "
"``--fixed-size`` option, the extra partition space is removed from the "
"filesystem size. Otherwise (with or without ``--size`` flag), the extra "
"partition space is added to the final partition size. The default value "
"is 0M. Specify as an integer value optionally followed by one of the "
"units \"k\" / \"K\" for kibibyte, \"M\" for mebibyte and \"G\" for "
"gibibyte. The default unit if none is given is \"M\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:169
msgid ""
"``--overhead-factor``: This option is a Wic-specific option that "
"multiplies the size of the partition by the option's value. You must "
"supply a value greater than or equal to \"1\". The default value is "
"\"1.3\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:174
msgid ""
"``--part-name``: This option is a Wic-specific option that specifies a "
"name for GPT partitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:177
msgid ""
"``--part-type``: This option is a Wic-specific option that specifies the "
"partition type globally unique identifier (GUID) for GPT partitions. You "
"can find the list of partition type GUIDs at "
":wikipedia:`GUID_Partition_Table#Partition_type_GUIDs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:182
msgid ""
"``--use-uuid``: This option is a Wic-specific option that causes Wic to "
"generate a random GUID for the partition. The generated identifier is "
"used in the bootloader configuration to specify the root partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:187
msgid ""
"``--uuid``: This option is a Wic-specific option that specifies the "
"partition UUID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:190
msgid ""
"``--fsuuid``: This option is a Wic-specific option that specifies the "
"filesystem UUID. You can generate or modify :term:`WKS_FILE` with this "
"option if a preconfigured filesystem UUID is added to the kernel command "
"line in the bootloader configuration before you run Wic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:196
msgid ""
"``--system-id``: This option is a Wic-specific option that specifies the "
"partition system ID, which is a one byte long, hexadecimal parameter with"
" or without the 0x prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:200
msgid ""
"``--mkfs-extraopts``: This option specifies additional options to pass to"
" the ``mkfs`` utility. Some default options for certain filesystems do "
"not take effect. See Wic's help on kickstart (i.e. ``wic help "
"kickstart``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:206
msgid "Command: bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:208
msgid ""
"This command specifies how the bootloader should be configured and "
"supports the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:213
msgid ""
"Bootloader functionality and boot partitions are implemented by the "
"various source plugins that implement bootloader functionality. The "
"bootloader command essentially provides a means of modifying bootloader "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:218
msgid ""
"``--append``: Specifies kernel parameters. These parameters will be added"
" to the syslinux :term:`APPEND` or ``grub`` kernel command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:221
msgid ""
"``--configfile``: Specifies a user-defined configuration file for the "
"bootloader. You can provide a full pathname for the file or a file "
"located in the ``files/wic`` folder. This option overrides all other "
"bootloader options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:226
msgid "``--ptable``: Specifies the partition table format. Valid values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:228
msgid "``msdos``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:230
msgid "``gpt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:232
msgid ""
"``--timeout``: Specifies the number of seconds before the bootloader "
"times out and boots the default option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:236
msgid "Directive: include"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/kickstart.rst:238
msgid ""
"The ``include`` directive can be used to include a WKS file into another."
" The only argument to this command is the path to the file to include, "
"relative to the current file. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:5
msgid "QA Error and Warning Messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:12
msgid ""
"When building a recipe, the OpenEmbedded build system performs various QA"
" checks on the output to ensure that common issues are detected and "
"reported. Sometimes when you create a new recipe to build new software, "
"it will build with no problems. When this is not the case, or when you "
"have QA issues building any software, it could take a little time to "
"resolve them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:19
msgid ""
"While it is tempting to ignore a QA message or even to disable QA checks,"
" it is best to try and resolve any reported QA issues. This chapter "
"provides a list of the QA messages and brief explanations of the issues "
"you could encounter so that you can properly resolve problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:24
msgid ""
"The next section provides a list of all QA error and warning messages "
"based on a default configuration. Each entry provides the message or "
"error form along with an explanation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:30
msgid ""
"At the end of each message, the name of the associated QA test (as listed"
" in the \":ref:`ref-classes-insane`\" section) appears within square "
"brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:34
msgid ""
"As mentioned, this list of error and warning messages is for QA checks "
"only. The list does not cover all possible build errors or warnings you "
"could encounter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:38
msgid ""
"Because some QA checks are disabled by default, this list does not "
"include all possible QA check errors and warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:44
msgid "Errors and Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:49
msgid "``already-stripped``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:51
msgid ""
"``File '<file>' from <recipename> was already stripped, this will prevent"
" future debugging! [already-stripped]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:53
msgid ""
"Produced binaries have already been stripped prior to the build system "
"extracting debug symbols. It is common for upstream software projects to "
"default to stripping debug symbols for output binaries. In order for "
"debugging to work on the target using ``-dbg`` packages, this stripping "
"must be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:59
msgid ""
"Depending on the build system used by the software being built, disabling"
" this stripping could be as easy as specifying an additional configure "
"option. If not, disabling stripping might involve patching the build "
"scripts. In the latter case, look for references to \"strip\" or "
"\"STRIP\", or the \"-s\" or \"-S\" command-line options being specified "
"on the linker command line (possibly through the compiler command line if"
" preceded with \"-Wl,\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:69
msgid ""
"Disabling stripping here does not mean that the final packaged binaries "
"will be unstripped. Once the OpenEmbedded build system splits out debug "
"symbols to the ``-dbg`` package, it will then strip the symbols from the "
"binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:77
msgid "``arch``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:79
msgid ""
"``Architecture did not match (<file_arch>, expected <machine_arch>) in "
"<file> [arch]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:81 ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:97
#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:113
msgid ""
"By default, the OpenEmbedded build system checks the Executable and "
"Linkable Format (ELF) type, bit size, and endianness of any binaries to "
"ensure they match the target architecture. This test fails if any "
"binaries do not match the type since there would be an incompatibility. "
"The test could indicate that the wrong compiler or compiler options have "
"been used. Sometimes software, like bootloaders, might need to bypass "
"this check. If the file you receive the error for is firmware that is not"
" intended to be executed within the target operating system or is "
"intended to run on a separate processor within the device, you can add "
"\"arch\" to :term:`INSANE_SKIP` for the package. Another option is to "
"check the :ref:`ref-tasks-compile` log and verify that the compiler "
"options being used are correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:95
msgid ""
"``Bit size did not match (<file_bits>, expected <machine_bits>) in <file>"
" [arch]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:111
msgid ""
"``Endianness did not match (<file_endianness>, expected "
"<machine_endianness>) in <file> [arch]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:130
msgid "``build-deps``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:132
msgid ""
"``<packagename1> rdepends on <packagename2>, but it isn't a build "
"dependency? [build-deps]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:134
msgid ""
"There is a runtime dependency between the two specified packages, but "
"there is nothing explicit within the recipe to enable the OpenEmbedded "
"build system to ensure that dependency is satisfied. This condition is "
"usually triggered by an :term:`RDEPENDS` value being added at the "
"packaging stage rather than up front, which is usually automatic based on"
" the contents of the package. In most cases, you should change the recipe"
" to add an explicit :term:`RDEPENDS` for the dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:146
msgid "``buildpaths``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:148
msgid ""
"``File <filename> in package <packagename> contains reference to TMPDIR "
"[buildpaths]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:150
msgid ""
"This check ensures that build system paths (including :term:`TMPDIR`) do "
"not appear in output files, which not only leaks build system "
"configuration into the target, but also hinders binary reproducibility as"
" the output will change if the build system configuration changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:155
msgid ""
"Typically these paths will enter the output through some mechanism in the"
" configuration or compilation of the software being built by the recipe. "
"To resolve this issue you will need to determine how the detected path is"
" entering the output. Sometimes it may require adjusting scripts or code "
"to use a relative path rather than an absolute one, or to pick up the "
"path from runtime configuration or environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:165
msgid "``configure-gettext``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:167
msgid "``AM_GNU_GETTEXT used but no inherit gettext [configure-gettext]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:169
msgid ""
"If a recipe is building something that uses automake and the automake "
"files contain an ``AM_GNU_GETTEXT`` directive then this check will fail "
"if there is no ``inherit gettext`` statement in the recipe to ensure that"
" gettext is available during the build. Add ``inherit gettext`` to remove"
" the warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:178
msgid "``configure-unsafe``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:180
msgid ""
"``This autoconf log indicates errors, it looked at host include and/or "
"library paths while determining system capabilities. Rerun configure task"
" after fixing this. [configure-unsafe]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:182
msgid ""
"The log for the :ref:`ref-tasks-configure` task indicates that paths on "
"the host were searched for files, which is not appropriate when cross-"
"compiling. Look for \"is unsafe for cross-compilation\" or \"CROSS "
"COMPILE Badness\" in the specified log file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:191
msgid "``debug-deps``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:193
msgid "``<packagename> rdepends on <debug_packagename> [debug-deps]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:195
msgid ""
"There is a dependency between the specified non-dbg package (i.e. a "
"package whose name does not end in ``-dbg``) and a package that is a "
"``dbg`` package. The ``dbg`` packages contain debug symbols and are "
"brought in using several different methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:200
msgid "Using the ``dbg-pkgs`` :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:203 ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:260
msgid "Using :term:`IMAGE_INSTALL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:205
msgid ""
"As a dependency of another ``dbg`` package that was brought in using one "
"of the above methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:208
msgid ""
"The dependency might have been automatically added because the ``dbg`` "
"package erroneously contains files that it should not contain (e.g. a "
"non-symlink ``.so`` file) or it might have been added manually (e.g. by "
"adding to :term:`RDEPENDS`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:216
msgid "``debug-files``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:218
msgid ""
"``non debug package contains .debug directory: <packagename> path <path> "
"[debug-files]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:220
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The specified package contains a ``.debug`` directory, which should not "
"appear in anything but the ``-dbg`` package. This situation might occur "
"if you add a path which contains a ``.debug`` directory and do not "
"explicitly add the ``.debug`` directory to the ``-dbg`` package. If this "
"is the case, add the ``.debug`` directory explicitly to "
"``FILES:${PN}-dbg``. See :term:`FILES` for additional information on "
":term:`FILES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:231
msgid "``dep-cmp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/qa-checks.rst:233
msgid ""
