msgid "``do_pydevshell``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:599
msgid ""
"Starts a shell in which an interactive Python interpreter allows you to "
"interact with the BitBake build environment. From within this shell, you "
"can directly examine and set bits from the data store and execute "
"functions as if within the BitBake environment. See the \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/python-development-shell:using a Python development shell`\" "
"section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for more "
"information about using ``pydevshell``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:609
msgid "``do_devshell``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:611
msgid ""
"Starts a shell whose environment is set up for development, debugging, or"
" both. See the \":ref:`dev-manual/development-shell:using a development "
"shell`\" section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for more "
"information about using ``devshell``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:619
msgid "``do_list_image_features``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:621
msgid ""
"Lists the available features for an image recipe. These features can be "
"set through either the :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` or "
":term:`EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:627
msgid "``do_listtasks``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:629
msgid "Lists all defined tasks for a target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:634
msgid "``do_package_index``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:636
msgid ""
"Creates or updates the index in the :ref:`overview-"
"manual/concepts:package feeds` area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:640
msgid ""
"This task is not triggered with the ``bitbake -c`` command-line option as"
" are the other tasks in this section. Because this task is specifically "
"for the ``package-index`` recipe, you run it using ``bitbake package-"
"index``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:645
msgid "Image-Related Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:647
msgid "The following tasks are applicable to image recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:652
msgid "``do_bootimg``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:654
msgid ""
"Creates a bootable live image. See the :term:`IMAGE_FSTYPES` variable for"
" additional information on live image types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:661
msgid "``do_bundle_initramfs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:663
msgid ""
"Combines an :term:`Initramfs` image and kernel together to form a single "
"image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:669
msgid "``do_rootfs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:671
msgid ""
"Creates the root filesystem (file and directory structure) for an image. "
"See the \":ref:`overview-manual/concepts:image generation`\" section in "
"the Yocto Project Overview and Concepts Manual for more information on "
"how the root filesystem is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:679
msgid "``do_testimage``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:681
msgid ""
"Boots an image and performs runtime tests within the image. For "
"information on automatically testing images, see the \":ref:`test-manual"
"/runtime-testing:performing automated runtime testing`\" section in the "
"Yocto Project Test Environment Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:689
msgid "``do_testimage_auto``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:691
msgid ""
"Boots an image and performs runtime tests within the image immediately "
"after it has been built. This task is enabled when you set "
":term:`TESTIMAGE_AUTO` equal to \"1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:695
msgid ""
"For information on automatically testing images, see the \":ref:`test-"
"manual/runtime-testing:performing automated runtime testing`\" section in"
" the Yocto Project Test Environment Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:700
msgid "Kernel-Related Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:702
msgid ""
"The following tasks are applicable to kernel recipes. Some of these tasks"
" (e.g. the :ref:`ref-tasks-menuconfig` task) are also applicable to "
"recipes that use Linux kernel style configuration such as the BusyBox "
"recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:710
msgid "``do_compile_kernelmodules``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:712
msgid ""
"Runs the step that builds the kernel modules (if needed). Building a "
"kernel consists of two steps: 1) the kernel (``vmlinux``) is built, and "
"2) the modules are built (i.e. ``make modules``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:719
msgid "``do_diffconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:721
msgid ""
"When invoked by the user, this task creates a file containing the "
"differences between the original config as produced by :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"kernel_configme` task and the changes made by the user with other methods"
" (i.e. using (:ref:`ref-tasks-menuconfig`). Once the file of differences "
"is created, it can be used to create a config fragment that only contains"
" the differences. You can invoke this task from the command line as "
"follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:732
msgid ""
"For more information, see the \":ref:`kernel-dev/common:creating "
"configuration fragments`\" section in the Yocto Project Linux Kernel "
"Development Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:739
msgid "``do_kernel_checkout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:741
msgid ""
"Converts the newly unpacked kernel source into a form with which the "
"OpenEmbedded build system can work. Because the kernel source can be "
"fetched in several different ways, the :ref:`ref-tasks-kernel_checkout` "
"task makes sure that subsequent tasks are given a clean working tree copy"
" of the kernel with the correct branches checked out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:750
msgid "``do_kernel_configcheck``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:752
msgid ""
"Validates the configuration produced by the :ref:`ref-tasks-menuconfig` "
"task. The :ref:`ref-tasks-kernel_configcheck` task produces warnings when"
" a requested configuration does not appear in the final ``.config`` file "
"or when you override a policy configuration in a hardware configuration "
"fragment. You can run this task explicitly and view the output by using "
"the following command::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:762
msgid ""
"For more information, see the \":ref:`kernel-dev/common:validating "
"configuration`\" section in the Yocto Project Linux Kernel Development "
"Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:769
msgid "``do_kernel_configme``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:771
msgid ""
"After the kernel is patched by the :ref:`ref-tasks-patch` task, the :ref"
":`ref-tasks-kernel_configme` task assembles and merges all the kernel "
"config fragments into a merged configuration that can then be passed to "
"the kernel configuration phase proper. This is also the time during which"
" user-specified defconfigs are applied if present, and where "
"configuration modes such as ``--allnoconfig`` are applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:781
msgid "``do_kernel_metadata``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:783
msgid ""
"Collects all the features required for a given kernel build, whether the "
"features come from :term:`SRC_URI` or from Git repositories. After "
"collection, the :ref:`ref-tasks-kernel_metadata` task processes the "
"features into a series of config fragments and patches, which can then be"
" applied by subsequent tasks such as :ref:`ref-tasks-patch` and :ref"
":`ref-tasks-kernel_configme`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:794
msgid "``do_menuconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:796
msgid ""
"Invoked by the user to manipulate the ``.config`` file used to build a "
"linux-yocto recipe. This task starts the Linux kernel configuration tool,"
" which you then use to modify the kernel configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:800
msgid "You can invoke this tool from the command line as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:806
msgid ""
"See the \":ref:`kernel-dev/common:using ``menuconfig```\" section in the "
"Yocto Project Linux Kernel Development Manual for more information on "
"this configuration tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:813
msgid "``do_savedefconfig``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:815
msgid ""
"When invoked by the user, creates a defconfig file that can be used "
"instead of the default defconfig. The saved defconfig contains the "
"differences between the default defconfig and the changes made by the "
"user using other methods (i.e. the :ref:`ref-tasks-menuconfig` task. You "
"can invoke the task using the following command::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:827
msgid "``do_shared_workdir``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:829
msgid ""
"After the kernel has been compiled but before the kernel modules have "
"been compiled, this task copies files required for module builds and "
"which are generated from the kernel build into the shared work directory."
" With these copies successfully copied, the :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"compile_kernelmodules` task can successfully build the kernel modules in "
"the next step of the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:839
msgid "``do_sizecheck``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:841
msgid ""
"If the variable :term:`KERNEL_IMAGE_MAXSIZE` is set, this task compares "
"the size of all stripped kernel images listed in "
":term:`KERNEL_IMAGETYPES` against that value. If more than one image type"
" is listed there, warn on any that exceed that value, but fail only if "
"none of them fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:849
msgid "``do_strip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:851
msgid ""
"If :term:`KERNEL_IMAGE_STRIP_EXTRA_SECTIONS` is defined, this task strips"
" the sections named in that variable from ``vmlinux``. This stripping is "
"typically used to remove nonessential sections such as ``.comment`` "
"sections from a size-sensitive configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:856
msgid "Common sections to strip:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:858
msgid "``.comment``: Holds compiler version strings and information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:860
msgid "``.note.*``: Extra notes often left by the compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:862
msgid "``.debug``: Debugging information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:867
msgid "``do_validate_branches``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/tasks.rst:869
msgid ""
"After the kernel is unpacked but before it is patched, this task makes "
"sure that the machine and metadata branches as specified by the "
":term:`SRCREV` variables actually exist on the specified branches. "
"Otherwise, if :term:`AUTOREV` is not being used, the :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"validate_branches` task fails during the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:5
msgid "Yocto Project Terms"
msgstr "Terminologia di Yocto Project"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:7
msgid ""
"Here is a list of terms and definitions users new to the Yocto Project "
"development environment might find helpful. While some of these terms are"
" universal, the list includes them just in case:"
msgstr "Ecco un elenco di termini e definizioni che potrebbero essere utili agli utenti che si avvicinano per la prima volta all'ambiente di sviluppo del Yocto Project. Sebbene alcuni di questi termini siano universali, l'elenco li include per completezza:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:12
msgid ":term:`Append Files`"
msgstr ":term:`File Append`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:14
msgid ""
"Files that append build information to a recipe file.  Append files are "
"known as BitBake append files and ``.bbappend`` files. The OpenEmbedded "
"build system expects every append file to have a corresponding recipe "
"(``.bb``) file. Furthermore, the append file and corresponding recipe "
"file must use the same root filename.  The filenames can differ only in "
"the file type suffix used (e.g. ``formfactor_0.0.bb`` and "
"``formfactor_0.0.bbappend``)."
msgstr "File che aggiungono informazioni di build a un file di ricetta. I file append sono noti come file append di BitBake e file ``.bbappend``. Il sistema di build OpenEmbedded prevede che ogni file append abbia un file di ricetta (``.bb``) corrispondente. Inoltre, il file append e il file ricetta corrispondente devono utilizzare lo stesso nome file radice. I nomi dei file possono differire solo per il suffisso del tipo di file utilizzato (ad esempio, ``formfactor_0.0.bb`` e ``formfactor_0.0.bbappend``)."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:22
msgid ""
"Information in append files extends or overrides the information in the "
"similarly-named recipe file. For an example of an append file in use, see"
" the    \":ref:`dev-manual/layers:appending other layers metadata with "
"your layer`\" section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr "Le informazioni contenute nei file append estendono o sovrascrivono le informazioni presenti nel file di ricetta con lo stesso nome. Per un esempio di file append in uso, consultare la sezione \":ref:`dev-manual/layers:appending other layers metadata with your layer`\" nel Manuale di Sviluppo dei Task di Yocto Project."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:27
msgid ""
"When you name an append file, you can use the \"``%``\" wildcard "
"character to allow for matching recipe names. For example, suppose you "
"have an append file named as follows::"
msgstr "Quando si assegna un nome a un file append, è possibile utilizzare il carattere jolly \"``%``\" per consentire la corrispondenza con i nomi delle ricette. Ad esempio, si supponga di avere un file append denominato come segue::"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:33
msgid ""
"That append file would match any ``busybox_1.21.x.bb`` version of the "
"recipe. So, the append file would match any of the following recipe "
"names:"
msgstr "Questo file append corrisponderà a qualsiasi versione della ricetta ``busybox_1.21.x.bb``. Quindi, il file append corrisponderà a uno qualsiasi dei seguenti nomi di ricetta:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:47
msgid ""
"The use of the \"%\" character is limited in that it only works directly "
"in front of the .bbappend portion of the append file's name. You cannot "
"use the wildcard character in any other location of the name."
msgstr "L'uso del carattere \"%\" è limitato al fatto che funziona solo direttamente prima della parte .bbappend del nome del file di append. Non è possibile utilizzare il carattere jolly in nessun'altra posizione del nome."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:51
msgid ":term:`BitBake`"
msgstr ":term:`BitBake`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:53
msgid ""
"The task executor and scheduler used by the OpenEmbedded build system to "
"build images. For more information on BitBake, see the :doc:`BitBake User"
" Manual <bitbake:index>`."
msgstr "L'esecutore e lo scheduler di task utilizzati dal sistema di build OpenEmbedded per creare le immagini. Per ulteriori informazioni su BitBake, consultare il :doc:`Manuale Utente di BitBake <bitbake:index>`."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:56
msgid ":term:`Board Support Package (BSP)`"
msgstr ":term:`Board Support Package (BSP)`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:58
msgid ""
"A group of drivers, definitions, and other components that provide "
"support for a specific hardware configuration. For more information on "
"BSPs, see the :doc:`/bsp-manual/index`."
msgstr "Un gruppo di driver, definizioni e altri componenti che forniscono supporto per una specifica configurazione hardware. Per ulteriori informazioni sui BSP, consultare il :doc:`/bsp-manual/index`."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:61
msgid ":term:`Build Directory`"
msgstr ":term:`Directory di Build`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:63
msgid ""
"This term refers to the area used by the OpenEmbedded build system for "
"builds. The area is created when you ``source`` the setup environment "
"script that is found in the Source Directory (i.e. :ref:`structure-core-"
"script`, or ``init-build-env`` when using :doc:`bitbake-setup <bitbake"
":bitbake-user-manual/bitbake-user-manual-environment-setup>`). The "
":term:`TOPDIR` variable points to the :term:`Build Directory`."
msgstr "Questo termine si riferisce all'area utilizzata dal sistema di compilazione OpenEmbedded per le build. L'area viene creata quando si esegue ``source`` lo script di configurazione dell'ambiente che si trova nella directory dei sorgenti (ad esempio, :ref:`structure-core-script` o ``init-build-env`` quando si utilizza :doc:`bitbake-setup <bitbake:bitbake-user-manual/bitbake-user-manual-environment-setup>`). La variabile :term:`TOPDIR` punta alla :term:`Build Directory`."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:71
msgid ""
"When setting up the build manually (see :doc:`/dev-manual/poky-manual-"
"setup`), you have a lot of flexibility when creating the :term:`Build "
"Directory`. Here are some examples that show how to create the directory."
"  The examples assume your :term:`Source Directory` is named ``bitbake-"
"builds``:"
msgstr "Quando si configura la build manualmente (vedere :doc:`/dev-manual/poky-manual-setup`), si ha molta flessibilità nella creazione della :term:`Build Directory`. Ecco alcuni esempi che mostrano come creare la directory. Gli esempi presuppongono che la :term:`Source Directory` si chiami ``bitbake-builds``:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:76
msgid ""
"Create the :term:`Build Directory` inside your Source Directory and let "
"the name of the :term:`Build Directory` default to ``build``:"
msgstr "Creare la :term:`Build Directory` all'interno della Source Directory e lascia che il nome predefinito della :term:`Build Directory` sia ``build``:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:84
msgid ""
"Or provide a path to the :term:`Build Directory` when sourcing ``oe-init-"
"build-env``. Any intermediate folders in the pathname must exist. This "
"next example creates a :term:`Build Directory` named ``YP-6.1`` within "
"the existing directory ``mybuilds``:"
msgstr "In alternativa, specifica il percorso della :term:`Build Directory` quando si esegue ``oe-init-build-env``. Tutte le cartelle intermedie nel path devono esistere. L'esempio seguente crea una :term:`Build Directory` denominata ``YP-6.1`` all'interno della directory esistente ``mybuilds``:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:93
msgid ""
"This path can also be an absolute path and be outside of the current "
"working directory:"
msgstr "Questo path può anche essere un percorso assoluto e trovarsi al di fuori della directory di lavoro corrente:"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:102
msgid ""
"By default, the :term:`Build Directory` contains :term:`TMPDIR`, which is"
" a temporary directory the build system uses for its work. :term:`TMPDIR`"
" cannot be under NFS. Thus, by default, the :term:`Build Directory` "
"cannot be under NFS. However, if you need the :term:`Build Directory` to "
"be under NFS, you can set this up by setting :term:`TMPDIR` in your :ref"
":`structure-build-conf-site.conf` file to use a local drive. Doing so "
"effectively separates :term:`TMPDIR` from :term:`TOPDIR`, which is the "
":term:`Build Directory`."
msgstr "Per default, la :term:`Build Directory` contiene :term:`TMPDIR`, una directory temporanea utilizzata dal sistema di compilazione. :term:`TMPDIR` non può trovarsi su un server NFS. Pertanto, per default, la :term:`Build Directory` non può trovarsi su un server NFS. Tuttavia, se è necessario che la :term:`Build Directory` si trovi su NFS, è possibile configurarla impostando :term:`TMPDIR` nel file :ref:`structure-build-conf-site.conf` in modo che utilizzi un'unità locale. In questo modo, :term:`TMPDIR` viene effettivamente separato da :term:`TOPDIR`, che rappresenta la :term:`Build Directory`."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:110
msgid ":term:`Build Host`"
msgstr ":term:`Host di Build`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:112
msgid ""
"The system used to build images in a Yocto Project Development "
"environment. The build system is sometimes referred to as the development"
" host."
msgstr "Il sistema utilizzato per creare immagini in un Ambiente di Aviluppo di Yocto Project. Il sistema di compilazione viene talvolta chiamato \"Host di Sviluppo\" o \"Build Host\"."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:115
msgid ":term:`buildtools`"
msgstr ":term:`buildtools`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:117
msgid ""
"Build tools in binary form, providing required versions of development "
"tools (such as Git, GCC, Python and make), to run the OpenEmbedded build "
"system on a development host without such minimum versions."
msgstr "Tool di compilazione in formato binario, che forniscono le versioni necessarie degli strumenti di sviluppo (come Git, GCC, Python e make) per eseguire il sistema di build di OpenEmbedded su un host di sviluppo che non dispone di tali versioni minime."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:121 ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:130
msgid ""
"See the \":ref:`system-requirements-buildtools`\" paragraph in the "
"Reference Manual for details about downloading or building an archive of "
"such tools."
msgstr "Consultare il paragrafo \":ref:`system-requirements-buildtools`\" nel Manuale di Riferimento per i dettagli sul download o la creazione di un archivio di tali strumenti."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:124
msgid ":term:`buildtools-extended`"
msgstr ":term:`buildtools-extended`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:126
msgid ""
"A set of :term:`buildtools` binaries extended with additional development"
" tools, such as a required version of the GCC compiler to run the "
"OpenEmbedded build system."
msgstr "Un set di binari :term:`buildtools` esteso con strumenti di sviluppo aggiuntivi, come una versione necessaria del compilatore GCC per eseguire il sistema di build di OpenEmbedded."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:133
msgid ":term:`buildtools-make`"
msgstr ":term:`buildtools-make`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:135
msgid ""
"A variant of :term:`buildtools`, just providing the required version of "
"``make`` to run the OpenEmbedded build system."
msgstr "Una variante di :term:`buildtools`, che fornisce solo la versione necessaria di ``make`` per eseguire il sistema di build di OpenEmbedded."

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:137
msgid ":term:`Built-in Fragment`"
msgstr ":term:`Built-in Fragment`"

#: ../../ref-manual/terms.rst:139
msgid ""
"A built-in fragment is a specific kind of :term:`Configuration Fragment` "
"that affects the value of a single variable globally. :term:`Built-in "
"Fragments <Built-in Fragment>` do not require a separate configuration "
"file, but like a standard :term:`Configuration Fragment`, Built-in "
"Fragments can be enabled or disabled using the :oe_git:`bitbake-config-"
"build </bitbake/tree/bin/bitbake-config-build>` command-line utility."
msgstr "Un built-in fragment [frammento nativo] è un tipo specifico di :term:`Configuration Fragment` che influenza il valore di una singola variabile a livello globale. I :term:`Built-in Fragments <Built-in Fragment>` non richiedono un file di configurazione separato, ma, come un normale :term:`Configuration Fragment`, possono essere abilitati o disabilitati tramite l'utilità da riga di comando :oe_git:`bitbake-config-build </bitbake/tree/bin/bitbake-config-build>`."

