#: ../../ref-manual/varlocality.rst:91
msgid ":term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:637
msgid ""
"The maximum number of tasks BitBake should run in parallel at any one "
"time. The OpenEmbedded build system automatically configures this "
"variable to be equal to the number of cores on the build system. For "
"example, a system with a dual core processor that also uses hyper-"
"threading causes the :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` variable to default to "
"\"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:644
msgid ""
"For single socket systems (i.e. one CPU), you should not have to override"
" this variable to gain optimal parallelism during builds. However, if you"
" have very large systems that employ multiple physical CPUs, you might "
"want to make sure the :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` variable is not set "
"higher than \"20\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:650 ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:7491
msgid ""
"For more information on speeding up builds, see the \":ref:`dev-manual"
"/speeding-up-build:speeding up a build`\" section in the Yocto Project "
"Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:654
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if your goal is to limit the amount of system "
"resources consumed by BitBake tasks, setting :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` to"
" a number lower than the number of CPU threads in your machine won't be "
"sufficient. That's because each package will still be built and installed"
" through a number of parallel jobs specified by the :term:`PARALLEL_MAKE`"
" variable, which is by default the number of CPU threads in your system, "
"and is not impacted by the :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:663
msgid ""
"So, if you set :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` to \"1\" but don't set "
":term:`PARALLEL_MAKE`, most of your system resources will be consumed "
"anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:667
msgid ""
"Therefore, if you intend to reduce the load of your build system by "
"setting :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` to a relatively low value compared to "
"the number of CPU threads on your system, you should also set "
":term:`PARALLEL_MAKE` to a similarly low value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:672
msgid ""
"An alternative to using :term:`BB_NUMBER_THREADS` to keep the usage of "
"build system resources under control is to use the smarter "
":term:`BB_PRESSURE_MAX_CPU`, :term:`BB_PRESSURE_MAX_IO` or "
":term:`BB_PRESSURE_MAX_MEMORY` controls. See the :doc:`/dev-manual"
"/limiting-resources` section of the Yocto Project Development Tasks "
"Manual."
msgstr ""

