#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-cargo` class, the variable "
":term:`CARGO_INSTALL_LIBRARIES` can be set to a non-empty value by "
"individual recipes to enable the installation of the libraries the recipe"
" has built in ``${B}/target/${CARGO_TARGET_SUBDIR}`` (files ending with "
"``.so`` or ``.rlib``). By default this variable is not defined and "
"libraries are not installed, to replicate the behavior of the ``cargo "
"install`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1522
msgid ":term:`CARGO_PROFILE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1524
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-cargo` class, the "
":term:`CARGO_PROFILE` variable allows selecting the profile to use when "
"building (``--profile`` option). By default this variable is "
"automatically set based on the value of :term:`DEBUG_BUILD`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1528
msgid ":term:`CC`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1530
msgid "The minimal command and arguments used to run the C compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1531
msgid ":term:`CCACHE_DISABLE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1533
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-ccache` class, the "
":term:`CCACHE_DISABLE` variable can be set to \"1\" in a recipe to "
"disable `Ccache` support. This is useful when the recipe is known to not "
"support it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1536
msgid ":term:`CCACHE_NATIVE_RECIPES_ALLOWED`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1538
msgid ""
"The :term:`CCACHE_NATIVE_RECIPES_ALLOWED` variable can be set in a "
":term:`configuration file` to a list of native recipes that are allowed "
"to be optimized with the :ref:`ref-classes-ccache` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1541
msgid ":term:`CCACHE_TOP_DIR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1543
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-ccache` class, the "
":term:`CCACHE_TOP_DIR` variable can be set to the location of where "
"`Ccache` stores its cache files. This directory can be shared between "
"builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1547
msgid ":term:`CCLD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1549
msgid ""
"The minimal command and arguments used to run the linker when the C "
"compiler is being used as the linker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1551
msgid ":term:`CFLAGS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1553
msgid ""
"Specifies the flags to pass to the C compiler. This variable is exported "
"to an environment variable and thus made visible to the software being "
"built during the compilation step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1557
msgid ""
"Default initialization for :term:`CFLAGS` varies depending on what is "
"being built:"
