msgid ":term:`CONFIGURE_FLAGS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1804
msgid "The minimal arguments for GNU configure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1805
msgid ":term:`CONFIGURE_SCRIPT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1807
msgid ""
"When using the :ref:`ref-classes-autotools` class, the "
":term:`CONFIGURE_SCRIPT` variable stores the location of the "
"``configure`` script for the Autotools build system. The default "
"definition for this variable is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1814
msgid ""
"Where :term:`AUTOTOOLS_SCRIPT_PATH` is the location of the of the "
"Autotools build system scripts, which defaults to :term:`S`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1816
msgid ":term:`CONFLICT_COMBINED_FEATURES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1818
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-features_check` class, this "
"variable identifies combined features (see :term:`COMBINED_FEATURES` for "
"what this means) that would be in conflict should the recipe be built. In"
" other words, if the :term:`CONFLICT_COMBINED_FEATURES` variable lists a "
"feature that also appears in :term:`COMBINED_FEATURES` within the current"
" configuration, then the recipe will be skipped, and if the build system "
"attempts to build the recipe then an error will be triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1828
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-features_check` class, this "
"variable identifies distro features that would be in conflict should the "
"recipe be built. In other words, if the :term:`CONFLICT_DISTRO_FEATURES` "
"variable lists a feature that also appears in :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` "
"within the current configuration, then the recipe will be skipped, and if"
" the build system attempts to build the recipe then an error will be "
"triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1835
msgid ":term:`CONFLICT_IMAGE_FEATURES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1837
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-features_check` class, this "
"variable identifies image features that would be in conflict should the "
"recipe be built. In other words, if the :term:`CONFLICT_IMAGE_FEATURES` "
"variable lists a feature that also appears in :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` "
"within the current configuration, then the recipe will be skipped, and if"
" the build system attempts to build the recipe then an error will be "
"triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1844
msgid ":term:`CONFLICT_MACHINE_FEATURES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1846
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-features_check` class, this "
"variable identifies machine features that would be in conflict should the"
" recipe be built. In other words, if the "
":term:`CONFLICT_MACHINE_FEATURES` variable lists a feature that also "
"appears in :term:`MACHINE_FEATURES` within the current configuration, "
"then the recipe will be skipped, and if the build system attempts to "
"build the recipe then an error will be triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1853
msgid ":term:`CONFLICT_TUNE_FEATURES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1855
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-features_check` class, this "
"variable identifies tune features that would be in conflict should the "
"recipe be built. In other words, if the :term:`CONFLICT_TUNE_FEATURES` "
"variable lists a feature that also appears in :term:`TUNE_FEATURES` "
"within the current configuration, then the recipe will be skipped, and if"
" the build system attempts to build the recipe then an error will be "
"triggered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1862
msgid ":term:`CONVERSION_CMD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1864
msgid ""
"This variable is used for storing image conversion commands. Image "
"conversion can convert an image into different objects like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1867
msgid "Compressed version of the image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1869
msgid "Checksums for the image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1871
msgid ""
"An example of :term:`CONVERSION_CMD` from :ref:`ref-classes-image_types` "
"class is::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1875
msgid ":term:`COPY_LIC_DIRS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1877
msgid ""
"If set to \"1\" along with the :term:`COPY_LIC_MANIFEST` variable, the "
"OpenEmbedded build system copies into the image the license files, which "
"are located in ``/usr/share/common-licenses``, for each package. The "
"license files are placed in directories within the image itself during "
"build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1886
msgid ""
"The :term:`COPY_LIC_DIRS` does not offer a path for adding licenses for "
"newly installed packages to an image, which might be most suitable for "
"read-only filesystems that cannot be upgraded. See the "
":term:`LICENSE_CREATE_PACKAGE` variable for additional information. You "
"can also reference the \":ref:`dev-manual/licenses:providing license "
"text`\" section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for "
"information on providing license text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1893
msgid ":term:`COPY_LIC_MANIFEST`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1895
msgid ""
"If set to \"1\", the OpenEmbedded build system copies the license "
"manifest for the image to ``/usr/share/common-licenses/license.manifest``"
" within the image itself during build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1902
msgid ""
"The :term:`COPY_LIC_MANIFEST` does not offer a path for adding licenses "
"for newly installed packages to an image, which might be most suitable "
"for read-only filesystems that cannot be upgraded. See the "
":term:`LICENSE_CREATE_PACKAGE` variable for additional information. You "
"can also reference the \":ref:`dev-manual/licenses:providing license "
"text`\" section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for "
"information on providing license text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1909
msgid ":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1911
msgid ""
"A space-separated list of licenses to exclude from the source archived by"
" the :ref:`ref-classes-archiver` class. In other words, if a license in a"
" recipe's :term:`LICENSE` value is in the value of "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE`, then its source is not archived by the "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1919
msgid ""
"The :term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE` variable takes precedence over the "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1922
msgid ""
"The default value, which is \"CLOSED Proprietary\", for "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE` is set by the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"copyleft_filter` class, which is inherited by the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"archiver` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1926
msgid ":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1928
msgid ""
"A space-separated list of licenses to include in the source archived by "
"the :ref:`ref-classes-archiver` class. In other words, if a license in a "
"recipe's :term:`LICENSE` value is in the value of "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE`, then its source is archived by the "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1934
msgid ""
"The default value is set by the :ref:`ref-classes-copyleft_filter` class,"
" which is inherited by the :ref:`ref-classes-archiver` class. The default"
" value includes \"GPL*\", \"LGPL*\", and \"AGPL*\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1937
msgid ":term:`COPYLEFT_PN_EXCLUDE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1939
msgid ""
"A list of recipes to exclude in the source archived by the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-archiver` class. The :term:`COPYLEFT_PN_EXCLUDE` variable "
"overrides the license inclusion and exclusion caused through the "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE` and :term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE` "
"variables, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1945
msgid ""
"The default value, which is \"\" indicating to not explicitly exclude any"
" recipes by name, for :term:`COPYLEFT_PN_EXCLUDE` is set by the :ref"
":`ref-classes-copyleft_filter` class, which is inherited by the :ref"
":`ref-classes-archiver` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1949
msgid ":term:`COPYLEFT_PN_INCLUDE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1951
msgid ""
"A list of recipes to include in the source archived by the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-archiver` class. The :term:`COPYLEFT_PN_INCLUDE` variable "
"overrides the license inclusion and exclusion caused through the "
":term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_INCLUDE` and :term:`COPYLEFT_LICENSE_EXCLUDE` "
"variables, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1957
msgid ""
"The default value, which is \"\" indicating to not explicitly include any"
" recipes by name, for :term:`COPYLEFT_PN_INCLUDE` is set by the :ref"
":`ref-classes-copyleft_filter` class, which is inherited by the :ref"
":`ref-classes-archiver` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1961
msgid ":term:`COPYLEFT_RECIPE_TYPES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1963
msgid ""
"A space-separated list of recipe types to include in the source archived "
"by the :ref:`archiver <ref-classes-archiver>` class. Recipe types are "
"``target``, :ref:`ref-classes-native`, :ref:`ref-classes-nativesdk`, :ref"
":`ref-classes-cross`, :ref:`ref-classes-crosssdk`, and :ref:`ref-classes-"
"cross-canadian`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:1969
msgid ""
"The default value, which is \"target*\", for "
