#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:4545
msgid ":term:`IMAGE_OVERHEAD_FACTOR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:4547
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Defines a multiplier that the build system applies to the initial image "
"size for cases when the multiplier times the returned disk usage value "
"for the image is greater than the sum of :term:`IMAGE_ROOTFS_SIZE` and "
":term:`IMAGE_ROOTFS_EXTRA_SPACE`. The result of the multiplier applied to"
" the initial image size creates free disk space in the image as overhead."
" By default, the build process uses a multiplier of 1.3 for this "
"variable. This default value results in 30% free disk space added to the "
"image when this method is used to determine the final generated image "
"size. You should be aware that post install scripts and the package "
"management system uses disk space inside this overhead area. "
"Consequently, the multiplier does not produce an image with all the "
"theoretical free disk space. See :term:`IMAGE_ROOTFS_SIZE` for "
"information on how the build system determines the overall image size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:4562
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The default 30% free disk space typically gives the image enough room to "
"boot and allows for basic post installs while still leaving a small "
"amount of free disk space. If 30% free space is inadequate, you can "
"increase the default value. For example, the following setting gives you "
"50% free space added to the image::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:4570
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can ensure a specific amount of free disk space is "
"added to the image by using the :term:`IMAGE_ROOTFS_EXTRA_SPACE` "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:4574
msgid ""
"When using Wic tool, beware that a second overhead factor is also "
"applied. This overhead value is defined by the ``--overhead-factor`` "
"option, which defaults to \"1.3\" when omitted. See the :ref:`ref-"
"manual/kickstart:command: part or partition` chapter in :doc:`/ref-"
"manual/kickstart` for details."
msgstr ""

