#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5437
msgid ":term:`KERNEL_CLASSES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5439
msgid ""
"A list of classes defining kernel image types that the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"kernel` class should inherit. You typically append this variable to "
"enable extended image types. You can register custom kernel image types "
"with the :ref:`ref-classes-kernel` class using this variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5444
msgid ":term:`KERNEL_CONSOLE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5446
msgid ""
"The :term:`KERNEL_CONSOLE` variable holds the value of the ``console`` "
"parameter of the kernel command line and can be used in places such as a "
"``wks`` description file for :ref:`Wic images <dev-manual/wic:creating "
"partitioned images using wic>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5451
msgid ""
"The default value of this variable is extracted from the first console "
"device and setting in :term:`SERIAL_CONSOLES`. If nothing is found in "
":term:`SERIAL_CONSOLES`, the default value is set to ``ttyS0,115200``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5455
msgid ""
"For more information, see the `Kernel command-line documentation "
"<https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-"
"parameters.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5457
msgid ":term:`KERNEL_DANGLING_FEATURES_WARN_ONLY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:5459
msgid ""
"When kernel configuration fragments are missing for some "
":term:`KERNEL_FEATURES` specified by layers or BSPs, building and "
"configuring the kernel stops with an error."
