msgid "SDK_POSTPROCESS_COMMAND += \"function\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9108
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If you need to pass an SDK path to a command within a function, you can "
"use ``${SDK_DIR}``, which points to the parent directory used by the "
"OpenEmbedded build system when creating SDK output. See the "
":term:`SDK_DIR` variable for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9112
msgid ":term:`SDK_PREFIX`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9114
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The toolchain binary prefix used for :ref:`ref-classes-nativesdk` "
"recipes. The OpenEmbedded build system uses the :term:`SDK_PREFIX` value "
"to set the :term:`TARGET_PREFIX` when building ``nativesdk`` recipes. The"
" default value is \"${SDK_SYS}-\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9119
msgid ":term:`SDK_RECRDEP_TASKS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9121
msgid ""
"A list of shared state tasks added to the extensible SDK. By default, the"
" following tasks are added:"
