#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9210
msgid ":term:`SDKEXTPATH`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9212
msgid ""
"The default installation directory for the Extensible SDK. By default, "
"this directory is based on the :term:`DISTRO` variable and is set in the "
":ref:`populate_sdk_base <ref-classes-populate-sdk-*>` class as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9220
msgid ""
"For the :term:`Poky` reference distro, the :term:`SDKEXTPATH` is set to "
"\"poky_sdk\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9223
msgid ""
"For information on how to change this default directory, see the \":ref"
":`sdk-manual/appendix-customizing:changing the default sdk installation "
"directory`\" section in the Yocto Project Application Development and the"
" Extensible Software Development Kit (eSDK) manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9227
msgid ":term:`SDKIMAGE_FEATURES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9229
msgid ""
"Equivalent to :term:`IMAGE_FEATURES`. However, this variable applies to "
"the SDK generated from an image using the following command::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9233
msgid ":term:`SDKMACHINE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9235
msgid ""
"The machine for which the SDK is built. In other words, the SDK is built "
"such that it runs on the target you specify with the :term:`SDKMACHINE` "
"value. The value points to a corresponding ``.conf`` file under ``conf"
"/machine-sdk/`` in the enabled layers, for example ``aarch64``, ``i586``,"
" ``i686``, ``ppc64``, ``ppc64le``, and ``x86_64`` are :oe_git:`available "
"in OpenEmbedded-Core </openembedded-core/tree/meta/conf/machine-sdk>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9242
msgid ""
"The variable defaults to :term:`BUILD_ARCH` so that SDKs are built for "
"the architecture of the build machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9247
msgid ""
"You cannot set the :term:`SDKMACHINE` variable in your distribution "
"configuration file. If you do, the configuration will not take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9250
msgid ":term:`SDKPATH`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9252
msgid ""
"Defines the path used to collect the SDK components and build the "
"installer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9254
msgid ":term:`SDKPATHINSTALL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9256
msgid ""
"Defines the path offered to the user for installation of the SDK that is "
"generated by the OpenEmbedded build system. The path appears as the "
"default location for installing the SDK when you run the SDK's "
"installation script. You can override the offered path when you run the "
"script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9261
msgid ":term:`SDKTARGETSYSROOT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9263
msgid ""
"The full path to the sysroot used for cross-compilation within an SDK as "
"it will be when installed into the default :term:`SDKPATHINSTALL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9266
