"Typically set in a distro :term:`configuration file` to apply globally to"
" all packages, or in a specific software recipe (or a ``.bbappend``) to "
"apply only to packages of that recipe. Recipe-level overrides "
"(``SPDX_PACKAGE_SUPPLIER:pn-<recipe>``) are also supported::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9886
msgid "See also :term:`SPDX_IMAGE_SUPPLIER` and :term:`SPDX_SDK_SUPPLIER`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9887
msgid ":term:`SPDX_PACKAGE_URL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9889
msgid ""
"Provides a place for the SPDX data creator to record the package URL "
"string (``software_packageUrl``), in accordance with the Package URL "
"specification) for a software Package. The default value of this variable"
" is an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9893
msgid ":term:`SPDX_PACKAGE_URLS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:9895
msgid ""
"A space-separated list of Package URLs (\"PURLs\") for the software "
"package. The first item in this list will be listed as the ``packageUrl``"
