#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10053
msgid ":term:`SRC_URI`"
msgstr ":term:`SRC_URI`"

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10056
msgid ""
"See the BitBake manual for the initial description for this variable: "
":term:`bitbake:SRC_URI`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10059
msgid "The following features are added by OpenEmbedded and the Yocto Project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10061
msgid "There are standard and recipe-specific options. Here are standard ones:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10063
msgid ""
"``apply`` --- whether to apply the patch or not. The default action is to"
" apply the patch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10066
msgid ""
"``striplevel`` --- which striplevel to use when applying the patch. The "
"default level is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10069
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``patchdir`` --- specifies the directory in which the patch should be "
"applied. The default is ``${``\\ :term:`S`\\ ``}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10072
msgid ""
"Here are options specific to recipes building code from a revision "
"control system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10075
msgid ""
"``mindate`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCDATE` is equal to or "
"greater than ``mindate``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10079
msgid ""
"``maxdate`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCDATE` is not later than"
" ``maxdate``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10082
msgid ""
"``minrev`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCREV` is equal to or "
"greater than ``minrev``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10085
msgid ""
"``maxrev`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCREV` is not later than "
"``maxrev``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10088
msgid "``rev`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCREV` is equal to ``rev``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10091
msgid ""
"``notrev`` --- apply the patch only if :term:`SRCREV` is not equal to "
"``rev``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10096
msgid ""
"If you want the build system to pick up files specified through a "
":term:`SRC_URI` statement from your append file, you need to be sure to "
"extend the :term:`FILESPATH` variable by also using the "
":term:`FILESEXTRAPATHS` variable from within your append file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10100
msgid ":term:`SRC_URI_OVERRIDES_PACKAGE_ARCH`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10102
msgid ""
"By default, the OpenEmbedded build system automatically detects whether "
":term:`SRC_URI` contains files that are machine-specific. If so, the "
"build system automatically changes :term:`PACKAGE_ARCH`. Setting this "
"variable to \"0\" disables this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10106
msgid ":term:`SRCDATE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10108
msgid ""
"The date of the source code used to build the package. This variable "
"applies only if the source was fetched from a Source Code Manager (SCM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10111
msgid ":term:`SRCPV`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10113
msgid ""
"The variable :term:`SRCPV` is deprecated. It was previously used to "
"include source control information in :term:`PV` for :term:`bitbake` to "
"work correctly but this is no longer a requirement. Source control "
"information will be automatically included by :term:`bitbake` in the "
"variable :term:`PKGV` during packaging if the ``+`` sign is present in "
":term:`PV`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10122
msgid ""
"The :term:`SRCPV` variable used to be defined in the "
"``meta/conf/bitbake.conf`` configuration file in :term:`OpenEmbedded-Core"
" (OE-Core)` as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10128
msgid ""
"The ``get_srcrev`` function can still be used to include source control "
"information in variables manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10130
msgid ":term:`SRCREV`"
msgstr ":term:`SRCREV`"

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10132
msgid ""
"The revision of the source code used to build the package. This variable "
"applies to Subversion, Git, and Mercurial only. Note that if you want to "
"build a fixed revision and you want to avoid performing a query on the "
"remote repository every time BitBake parses your recipe, you should "
"specify a :term:`SRCREV` that is a full revision identifier (e.g. the "
"full SHA hash in git) and not just a tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10141
msgid ""
"For information on limitations when inheriting the latest revision of "
"software using :term:`SRCREV`, see the :term:`AUTOREV` variable "
"description and the \":ref:`dev-manual/packages:automatically "
"incrementing a package version number`\" section, which is in the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10146
msgid ":term:`SRCREV_FORMAT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10148
msgid "See :term:`bitbake:SRCREV_FORMAT` in the BitBake manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10149
msgid ":term:`SRCTREECOVEREDTASKS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10151
msgid ""
"A list of tasks that are typically not relevant (and therefore skipped) "
"when building using the :ref:`ref-classes-externalsrc` class. The default"
" value as set in that class file is the set of tasks that are rarely "
"needed when using external source::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10158
msgid ""
"The notable exception is when processing external kernel source as "
"defined in the :ref:`ref-classes-kernel-yocto` class file (formatted for "
"aesthetics)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10171
msgid ""
"See the associated :term:`EXTERNALSRC` and :term:`EXTERNALSRC_BUILD` "
"variables for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10173
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_DIR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10175
msgid "The directory for the shared state cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10176
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_EXCLUDEDEPS_SYSROOT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10178
msgid ""
"This variable allows to specify indirect dependencies to exclude from "
"sysroots, for example to avoid the situations when a dependency on any "
"``-native`` recipe will pull in all dependencies of that recipe in the "
"recipe sysroot. This behaviour might not always be wanted, for example "
"when that ``-native`` recipe depends on build tools that are not relevant"
" for the current recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10185
msgid ""
"This way, irrelevant dependencies are ignored, which could have prevented"
" the reuse of prebuilt artifacts stored in the Shared State Cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10189
msgid ""
":term:`SSTATE_EXCLUDEDEPS_SYSROOT` is evaluated as two regular "
"expressions of recipe and dependency to ignore. An example is the rule in"
" :oe_git:`meta/conf/layer.conf </openembedded-"
"core/tree/meta/conf/layer.conf>`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10200
msgid ""
"The ``->`` substring represents the dependency between the two regular "
"expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10202
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_MIRROR_ALLOW_NETWORK`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10204
msgid ""
"If set to \"1\", allows fetches from mirrors that are specified in "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` to work even when fetching from the network is "
"disabled by setting :term:`BB_NO_NETWORK` to \"1\". Using the "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRROR_ALLOW_NETWORK` variable is useful if you have set "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` to point to an internal server for your shared "
"state cache, but you want to disable any other fetching from the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10211
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10213
msgid ""
"Configures the OpenEmbedded build system to search other mirror locations"
" for prebuilt cache data objects before building out the data. This "
"variable works like fetcher :term:`MIRRORS` and :term:`PREMIRRORS` and "
"points to the cache locations to check for the shared state (sstate) "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10219
msgid ""
"You can specify a filesystem directory or a remote URL such as HTTP or "
"FTP. The locations you specify need to contain the shared state cache "
"(sstate-cache) results from previous builds. The sstate-cache you point "
"to can also be from builds on other machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10224
msgid ""
"The Yocto Project actually shares the cache data objects built by its "
"autobuilder::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10229
msgid ""
"As such binary artifacts are built for the generic QEMU machines "
"supported by the various Poky releases, they are less likely to be "
"reusable in real projects building binaries optimized for a specific CPU "
"family."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10234
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`/dev-manual/sstate-mirrors-setup` section of the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual for details on how to setup a shared "
"state mirror."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10237
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_SCAN_FILES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10239
msgid ""
"Controls the list of files the OpenEmbedded build system scans for "
"hardcoded installation paths. The variable uses a space-separated list of"
" filenames (not paths) with standard wildcard characters allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10244
msgid ""
"During a build, the OpenEmbedded build system creates a shared state "
"(sstate) object during the first stage of preparing the sysroots. That "
"object is scanned for hardcoded paths for original installation "
"locations. The list of files that are scanned for paths is controlled by "
"the :term:`SSTATE_SCAN_FILES` variable. Typically, recipes add files they"
" want to be scanned to the value of :term:`SSTATE_SCAN_FILES` rather than"
" the variable being comprehensively set. The :ref:`ref-classes-sstate` "
"class specifies the default list of files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10253
msgid "For details on the process, see the :ref:`ref-classes-staging` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10254
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_SIG_KEY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10256
msgid ""
"When signing :ref:`shared state <overview-manual/concepts:setscene tasks "
"and shared state>` artifacts (when :term:`SSTATE_VERIFY_SIG` is set to "
"\"1\"), the :term:`SSTATE_SIG_KEY` variable is the :wikipedia:`GPG "
"<GNU_Privacy_Guard>` key identifier used to sign them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10261 ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10270
#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10319 ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10327
msgid ""
"See :doc:`/security-manual/sstate-signing` in the Yocto Project Security "
"Manual for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10263
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_SIG_PASSPHRASE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10265
msgid ""
"When signing :ref:`shared state <overview-manual/concepts:setscene tasks "
"and shared state>` artifacts (when :term:`SSTATE_VERIFY_SIG` is set to "
"\"1\"), the :term:`SSTATE_SIG_PASSPHRASE` variable is the passphrase used"
" to protect the private key signing the artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10272
msgid ":term:`SSTATE_SKIP_CREATION`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10274
msgid ""
"The :term:`SSTATE_SKIP_CREATION` variable can be used to skip the "
"creation of :ref:`shared state <overview-manual/concepts:shared state "
"cache>` tarball files. It makes sense e.g. for image creation tasks as "
"tarring images and keeping them in sstate would consume a lot of disk "
"space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:10279
msgid ""
"In general it is not recommended to use this variable as missing sstate "
"artefacts adversely impact the build, particularly for entries in the "
