#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12293
msgid "The default U-Boot extension is ``.bin``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12294
msgid ":term:`UBOOT_TARGET`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12296
msgid ""
"Specifies the target used for building U-Boot. The target is passed "
"directly as part of the \"make\" command (e.g. SPL and AIS). If you do "
"not specifically set this variable, the OpenEmbedded build process passes"
" and uses \"all\" for the target during the U-Boot building process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12301
msgid ":term:`UBOOT_VERSION`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12303
msgid ""
"When naming the files that are installed and deployed, the package "
"version (:term:`PV`) and revision (:term:`PR`) are part of the filename. "
"The :term:`UBOOT_VERSION` variable contains this information, but can be "
"overridden if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12307
msgid ":term:`UKI_CMDLINE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12309
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, the kernel command line"
" to use when booting the `Unified Kernel Image (UKI) <https://uapi-"
"group.org/specifications/specs/unified_kernel_image/>`__. Defaults to "
"``rootwait root=LABEL=root console=${KERNEL_CONSOLE}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12313
msgid ":term:`UKI_CONFIG_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12315
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, an optional config file"
" for the `ukify "
"<https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/ukify.html>`__ "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12319
msgid ":term:`UKI_DEVICETREE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12321
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, the "
":term:`UKI_DEVICETREE` variable holds the list of device tree blobs to "
"include in the `Unified Kernel Image (UKI) <https://uapi-"
"group.org/specifications/specs/unified_kernel_image/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12324
msgid ":term:`UKI_FILENAME`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12326
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, the output file name "
"for the generated `Unified Kernel Image (UKI) <https://uapi-"
"group.org/specifications/specs/unified_kernel_image/>`__. Defaults to "
"``uki.efi``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12330
msgid ":term:`UKI_KERNEL_FILENAME`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12332
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, the kernel image file "
"name to use as input. Defaults to :term:`KERNEL_IMAGETYPE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12334
msgid ":term:`UKI_SB_CERT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12336
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, optional UEFI "
"secureboot certificate matching the private key in :term:`UKI_SB_KEY`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12338
msgid ":term:`UKI_SB_KEY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12340
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, optional UEFI "
"secureboot private key to sign the `Unified Kernel Image (UKI) <https"
"://uapi-group.org/specifications/specs/unified_kernel_image/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12343
msgid ":term:`UKIFY_CMD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12345
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uki` class, `ukify "
"<https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/ukify.html>`__ "
"command to build `Unified Kernel Image (UKI) <https://uapi-"
"group.org/specifications/specs/unified_kernel_image/>`__. Defaults to "
"``ukify build``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12349
msgid ":term:`UNINATIVE_CHECKSUM`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12351
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uninative` class, the "
":term:`UNINATIVE_CHECKSUM` variable flags contain the checksums of the "
"uninative tarball as specified by the :term:`UNINATIVE_URL` variable. "
"There should be one checksum per tarballs published at "
":term:`UNINATIVE_URL`, which match architectures. For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12360
msgid ":term:`UNINATIVE_URL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12362
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-uninative` class, the "
":term:`UNINATIVE_URL` variable contains the URL where the uninative "
"tarballs are published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12365
msgid ":term:`UNKNOWN_CONFIGURE_OPT_IGNORE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12367
msgid ""
"Specifies a list of options that, if reported by the configure script as "
"being invalid, should not generate a warning during the :ref:`ref-tasks-"
"configure` task. Normally, invalid configure options are simply not "
"passed to the configure script (e.g. should be removed from "
":term:`EXTRA_OECONF` or :term:`PACKAGECONFIG_CONFARGS`). However, there "
"are common options that are passed to all configure scripts at a class "
"level, but might not be valid for some configure scripts. Therefore "
"warnings about these options are useless. For these cases, the options "
"are added to :term:`UNKNOWN_CONFIGURE_OPT_IGNORE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12378
msgid ""
"The configure arguments check that uses "
":term:`UNKNOWN_CONFIGURE_OPT_IGNORE` is part of the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"insane` class and is only enabled if the recipe inherits the :ref:`ref-"
"classes-autotools` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12382
msgid ":term:`UNPACKDIR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12384
msgid ""
"This variable, used by the :ref:`ref-classes-base` class, specifies where"
" fetched sources should be unpacked by the :ref:`ref-tasks-unpack` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12387
msgid ":term:`UPDATERCPN`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12389
msgid ""
"For recipes inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-update-rc.d` class, "
":term:`UPDATERCPN` specifies the package that contains the initscript "
"that is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12393
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The default value is \"${PN}\". Given that almost all recipes that "
"install initscripts package them in the main package for the recipe, you "
"rarely need to set this variable in individual recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12396
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_COMMITS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12398
msgid ""
"You can perform a per-recipe check for what the latest upstream source "
"code version is by calling ``devtool latest-version recipe``. If the "
"recipe source code is provided from Git repositories, but releases are "
"not identified by Git tags, set :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_COMMITS` to ``1`` "
"in the recipe, and the OpenEmbedded build system will compare the latest "
"commit with the one currently specified by the recipe (:term:`SRCREV`)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12407
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_GITTAGREGEX`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12409
msgid ""
"You can perform a per-recipe check for what the latest upstream source "
"code version is by calling ``devtool latest-version recipe``. If the "
"recipe source code is provided from Git repositories, the OpenEmbedded "
"build system determines the latest upstream version by picking the latest"
" tag from the list of all repository tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12415
msgid ""
"You can use the :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_GITTAGREGEX` variable to provide a "
"regular expression to filter only the relevant tags should the default "
"filter not work correctly::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12420
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_REGEX`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12422
msgid ""
"Use the :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_REGEX` variable to specify a different "
"regular expression instead of the default one when the package checking "
"system is parsing the page found using :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_URI`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12428
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_URI`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12430
msgid ""
"You can perform a per-recipe check for what the latest upstream source "
"code version is by calling ``devtool latest-version recipe``. If the "
"source code is provided from tarballs, the latest version is determined "
"by fetching the directory listing where the tarball is and attempting to "
"find a later tarball. When this approach does not work, you can use "
":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_URI` to provide a different URI that contains the "
"link to the latest tarball::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12439
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_STABLE_RELEASE_REGEX`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12441
msgid ""
"A regular expression used to filter upstream versions during version "
"checks so that only versions within the same stable series are "
"considered. When set, BitBake's fetchers (git, wget, crate) apply this "
"regex to discovered upstream versions and discard any that do not match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12446
msgid ""
"For example, if a recipe is at version ``1.4.2`` and the regex is "
"``^1\\.4(\\.\\d+)*$``, then ``1.4.7`` would be a valid upgrade candidate "
"but ``1.5.0`` would not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12450
msgid ""
"For recipes with dot-separated versions, inherit the :ref:`ref-classes-"
"upstream-stable-release-point` class to generate this variable "
"automatically. For other versioning schemes, set it directly::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12456
msgid ""
"See :ref:`ref-manual/release-process:stable point release upgrades` for "
"the criteria under which this variable should be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12458
msgid ":term:`UPSTREAM_VERSION_UNKNOWN`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12460
msgid ""
"You can perform a per-recipe check for what the latest upstream source "
"code version is by calling ``devtool latest-version recipe``. If no "
"combination of the :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_URI`, "
":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_REGEX`, :term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_GITTAGREGEX` and "
":term:`UPSTREAM_CHECK_COMMITS` variables in the recipe allows to "
"determine what the latest upstream version is, you can set "
":term:`UPSTREAM_VERSION_UNKNOWN` to ``1`` in the recipe to acknowledge "
"that the check cannot be performed::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12469
msgid ":term:`USE_DEVFS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12471
msgid ""
"Determines if ``devtmpfs`` is used for ``/dev`` population. The default "
"value used for :term:`USE_DEVFS` is \"1\" when no value is specifically "
"set. Typically, you would set :term:`USE_DEVFS` to \"0\" for a statically"
" populated ``/dev`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12476
msgid ""
"See the \":ref:`dev-manual/device-manager:selecting a device manager`\" "
"section in the Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual for information on "
"how to use this variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12479
msgid ":term:`USE_NLS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12481
msgid ""
"Determine if language translations should be built for recipes that can "
"build them. This variable can be equal to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12484
msgid "``yes``: translations are enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12485
msgid "``no``: translation are disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12487
msgid ""
"Recipes can use the value of this variable to enable language "
"translations in their build. Classes such as :ref:`ref-classes-gettext` "
"use the value of this variable to enable :wikipedia:`Gettext <Gettext>` "
"support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12491
msgid ":term:`USE_VT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12493
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`SysVinit <dev-manual/new-recipe:enabling system "
"services>`, determines whether or not to run a :wikipedia:`getty "
"<Getty_(Unix)>` on any virtual terminals in order to enable logging in "
"through those terminals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12499
msgid ""
"The default value used for :term:`USE_VT` is \"1\" when no default value "
"is specifically set. Typically, you would set :term:`USE_VT` to \"0\" in "
"the machine configuration file for machines that do not have a graphical "
"display attached and therefore do not need virtual terminal "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12504
msgid ":term:`USER_CLASSES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12506
msgid ""
"A list of classes to globally inherit. These classes are used by the "
"OpenEmbedded build system to enable extra features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12509
msgid ""
"Classes inherited using :term:`USER_CLASSES` must be located in the "
"``classes-global/`` or ``classes/`` subdirectories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12512
msgid ""
"A default list is set in the "
":oecore_path:`meta/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample` file::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12516
msgid ":term:`USERADD_DEPENDS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12518
msgid ""
"Specifies a list of recipes that create users / groups (via "
":term:`USERADD_PARAM` / :term:`GROUPADD_PARAM`) which a recipe depends "
"upon. This ensures that those users / groups are available when building "
"a recipe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12522
msgid ":term:`USERADD_ERROR_DYNAMIC`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12524
msgid ""
"If set to ``error``, forces the OpenEmbedded build system to produce an "
"error if the user identification (``uid``) and group identification "
"(``gid``) values are not defined in any of the files listed in "
":term:`USERADD_UID_TABLES` and :term:`USERADD_GID_TABLES`. If set to "
"``warn``, a warning will be issued instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12531
msgid ""
"The default behavior for the build system is to dynamically apply ``uid``"
" and ``gid`` values. Consequently, the :term:`USERADD_ERROR_DYNAMIC` "
"variable is by default not set. If you plan on using statically assigned "
"``gid`` and ``uid`` values, you should set the "
":term:`USERADD_ERROR_DYNAMIC` variable in a :term:`configuration file`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12540
msgid ""
"Overriding the default behavior implies you are going to also take steps "
"to set static ``uid`` and ``gid`` values through use of the "
":term:`USERADDEXTENSION`, :term:`USERADD_UID_TABLES`, and "
":term:`USERADD_GID_TABLES` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12549
msgid ""
"There is a difference in behavior between setting "
":term:`USERADD_ERROR_DYNAMIC` to ``error`` and setting it to ``warn``. "
"When it is set to ``warn``, the build system will report a warning for "
"every undefined ``uid`` and ``gid`` in any recipe. But when it is set to "
"``error``, it will only report errors for recipes that are actually "
"built. This saves you from having to add static IDs for recipes that you "
"know will never be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12557
msgid ":term:`USERADD_GID_TABLES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12559
msgid ""
"Specifies a password file to use for obtaining static group "
"identification (``gid``) values when the OpenEmbedded build system adds a"
" group to the system during package installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12563
msgid ""
"When applying static group identification (``gid``) values, the "
"OpenEmbedded build system looks in :term:`BBPATH` for a ``files/group`` "
"file and then applies those ``uid`` values. Set the variable as follows "
"in a :term:`configuration file`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12572
msgid ""
"Setting the :term:`USERADDEXTENSION` variable to \"useradd-staticids\" "
"causes the build system to use static ``gid`` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12574
msgid ":term:`USERADD_PACKAGES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12576
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-useradd` class, this variable "
"specifies the individual packages within the recipe that require users "
"and/or groups to be added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12580
msgid ""
"You must set this variable if the recipe inherits the class. For example,"
" the following enables adding a user for the main package in a recipe::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12588
msgid ""
"It follows that if you are going to use the :term:`USERADD_PACKAGES` "
"variable, you need to set one or more of the :term:`USERADD_PARAM`, "
":term:`GROUPADD_PARAM`, or :term:`USERMOD_PARAM` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12591
msgid ":term:`USERADD_PARAM`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12593
msgid ""
"When inheriting the :ref:`ref-classes-useradd` class, this variable "
"specifies for a package what parameters should pass to the ``useradd`` "
"command if you add a user to the system when the package is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12604
msgid ""
"For information on the standard Linux shell command ``useradd``, see "
":manpage:`useradd(8)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12607
msgid ":term:`USERADD_UID_TABLES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12609
msgid ""
"Specifies a password file to use for obtaining static user identification"
" (``uid``) values when the OpenEmbedded build system adds a user to the "
"system during package installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12613
msgid ""
"When applying static user identification (``uid``) values, the "
"OpenEmbedded build system looks in :term:`BBPATH` for a ``files/passwd`` "
"file and then applies those ``uid`` values. Set the variable as follows "
"in a :term:`configuration file`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12622
msgid ""
"Setting the :term:`USERADDEXTENSION` variable to \"useradd-staticids\" "
"causes the build system to use static ``uid`` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12624
msgid ":term:`USERADDEXTENSION`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12626
msgid ""
"When set to \"useradd-staticids\", causes the OpenEmbedded build system "
"to base all user and group additions on a static ``passwd`` and ``group``"
" files found in :term:`BBPATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12630
msgid ""
"To use static user identification (``uid``) and group identification "
"(``gid``) values, set the variable as follows in in a "
":term:`configuration file`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12638
msgid ""
"Setting this variable to use static ``uid`` and ``gid`` values causes the"
" OpenEmbedded build system to employ the :ref:`ref-classes-useradd` "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12642
msgid ""
"If you use static ``uid`` and ``gid`` information, you must also specify "
"the ``files/passwd`` and ``files/group`` files by setting the "
":term:`USERADD_UID_TABLES` and :term:`USERADD_GID_TABLES` variables. "
"Additionally, you should also set the :term:`USERADD_ERROR_DYNAMIC` "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12648
msgid ":term:`USERMOD_PARAM`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12650
msgid ""
"When a recipe inherits the :ref:`ref-classes-useradd` class, this "
"variable specifies for a package what parameters should be passed to the "
"``usermod`` command if you wish to modify a user when the package is "
"installed. Is is typically used to add the user to one or more groups. "
"For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12656
msgid ":term:`VIRTUAL-RUNTIME`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12658
msgid ""
":term:`VIRTUAL-RUNTIME` is a commonly used prefix for defining virtual "
"packages for runtime usage, typically for use in :term:`RDEPENDS` or in "
"image definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12662
msgid ""
"An example is ``VIRTUAL-RUNTIME_base-utils`` that makes it possible to "
"either use BusyBox based utilities::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12667
msgid ""
"or their full featured implementations from GNU Coreutils and other "
"projects::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12672
msgid ""
"Here are two examples using this virtual runtime package. The first one "
"is in :oe_git:`initramfs-framework_1.0.bb </openembedded-core/tree/meta"
"/recipes-core/initrdscripts/initramfs-framework_1.0.bb>`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12678
msgid ""
"The second example is in the :oe_git:`core-image-initramfs-boot "
"</openembedded-core/tree/meta/recipes-core/images/core-image-initramfs-"
"boot.bb>` image definition::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12683
msgid ":term:`WARN_QA`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12685
msgid ""
"Specifies the quality assurance checks whose failures are reported as "
"warnings by the OpenEmbedded build system. You set this variable in your "
"distribution configuration file. For a list of the checks you can control"
" with this variable, see the \":ref:`ref-classes-insane`\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12690
msgid ":term:`WATCHDOG_RUNTIME_SEC`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12692
msgid ""
"For the ``systemd`` recipe, this controls the value of the "
"``RuntimeWatchdogSec`` option in ``/etc/systemd/system.conf``. The "
"default value is an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12695
msgid ":term:`WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12697
msgid ""
"Specifies the timeout in seconds used by the ``watchdog-config`` recipe "
"and also by ``systemd`` during reboot. The default is 60 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12699
msgid ":term:`WESTON_USER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12701
msgid ""
"The :term:`WESTON_USER` variable defines the username for the `Weston` "
"user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12703
msgid ":term:`WESTON_USER_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12705
msgid ""
"The :term:`WESTON_USER` variable defines the path to the home directory "
"for the `Weston` user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12707
msgid ":term:`WIC_CREATE_EXTRA_ARGS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12709
msgid ""
"If the :term:`IMAGE_FSTYPES` variable contains \"wic\", the build will "
"generate a :ref:`Wic image <dev-manual/wic:creating partitioned images "
"using wic>` automatically when BitBake builds an image recipe. As part of"
" this process BitBake will invoke the \"`wic create`\" command. The "
":term:`WIC_CREATE_EXTRA_ARGS` variable is placed at the end of this "
"command which allows the user to supply additional arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12717
msgid ""
"One such useful purpose for this mechanism is to add the ``-D`` (or "
"``--debug``) argument to the \"`wic create`\" command. This increases the"
" amount of debugging information written out to the Wic log during the "
"Wic creation process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12721
msgid ":term:`WIC_SECTOR_SIZE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12726
msgid ""
"This variable is deprecated in favor of the ``--sector-size`` wic "
"command-line argument. See :ref:`ref-migration-6-0-wic-sector-size-"
"change` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12730
msgid ""
"The variable :term:`WIC_SECTOR_SIZE` controls the sector size of Wic "
"images. In the background, this controls the value of the "
"``PARTED_SECTOR_SIZE`` environment variable passed to the ``parted`` "
"command-line utility, used to generated the images. The default value is "
"``512``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12736
msgid ""
"For more information on how to create Wic images, see the \":ref:`dev-"
"manual/wic:creating partitioned images using wic`\" section in the Yocto "
"Project Development Tasks Manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12739
msgid ":term:`WIRELESS_DAEMON`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12741
msgid ""
"For ``connman`` and ``packagegroup-base``, specifies the wireless daemon "
"to use. The default is \"wpa-supplicant\" (note that the value uses a "
"dash and not an underscore)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12744
msgid ":term:`WKS_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12746
msgid ""
"Specifies the location of the Wic kickstart file that is used by the "
"OpenEmbedded build system to create a partitioned image (``image.wic``). "
"For information on how to create a partitioned image, see the \":ref"
":`dev-manual/wic:creating partitioned images using wic`\" section in the "
"Yocto Project Development Tasks Manual. For details on the kickstart file"
" format, see the \":doc:`/ref-manual/kickstart`\" Chapter."
