#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12762
msgid ""
"The :term:`WKS_FILE_DEPENDS` variable is similar to the :term:`DEPENDS` "
"variable. When you use the variable in your recipe that builds the Wic "
"image, dependencies you list in the :term:`WKS_FILE_DEPENDS` variable are"
" added to the :term:`DEPENDS` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12767
msgid ""
"With the :term:`WKS_FILE_DEPENDS` variable, you have the possibility to "
"specify a list of additional dependencies (e.g. native tools, "
"bootloaders, and so forth), that are required to build Wic images. Here "
"is an example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12774
msgid ""
"In the previous example, some-native-tool would be replaced with an "
"actual native tool on which the build would depend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12777
msgid ":term:`WKS_FILES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12779
msgid ""
"Specifies a list of candidate Wic kickstart files to be used by the "
"OpenEmbedded build system to create a partitioned image. Only the first "
"one that is found, from left to right, will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12783
msgid ""
"This is only useful when there are multiple ``.wks`` files that can be "
"used to produce an image. A typical case is when multiple layers are used"
" for different hardware platforms, each supplying a different ``.wks`` "
"file. In this case, you specify all possible ones through "
":term:`WKS_FILES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ref-manual/variables.rst:12789
msgid "If only one ``.wks`` file is used, set :term:`WKS_FILE` instead."
msgstr ""

